{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760626146,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e011ce67001k9tym8rC9l9487","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e011b9e8001yDh43PVgsD09dy","type":"tool","id":"call_bf513130e17e48cca0a3ba9c","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 1-218\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review Strategy Template\n3: description: Runtime template copied to review/ during initialization to track review progress, dimension coverage, findings, and outcomes across iterations.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review strategy template\"\n6:   - \"review dimension tracking\"\n7:   - \"exhausted review approaches\"\n8:   - \"review session tracking\"\n9: importance_tier: normal\n10: contextType: planning\n11: version: 1.11.0.13\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # Deep Review Strategy - Session Tracking Template\n15: \n16: Runtime template copied into the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` during initialization. Tracks review progress across iterations.\n17: \n18: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n19: \n20: ### Purpose\n21: \n22: Serves as the \"persistent brain\" for a deep review session. Records which dimensions remain, what was found (P0/P1/P2), what review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read by the orchestrator and agents at every iteration.\n23: \n24: ### Usage\n25: \n26: - **Init:** Orchestrator copies this template to `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-strategy.md` and populates Topic, Review Dimensions, Known Context, and Review Boundaries from config and memory context.\n27: - **Per iteration:** Agent reads Next Focus, reviews the assigned dimension/files, updates findings, marks dimensions complete, and sets new Next Focus.\n28: - **Mutability:** Mutable, updated by both orchestrator and agents throughout the session.\n29: - **Protection:** None (shared mutable state). Orchestrator validates consistency on resume.\n30: - **Ownership:** Machine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human commentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n31: \n32: ---\n33: \n34: ## 2. TOPIC\n35: [Review target description from config -- set during initialization]\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n40: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n41: - [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n42: - [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n43: - [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n44: - [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n45: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n50: [What this review session is NOT trying to assess -- populated during initialization]\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n55: [Explicit conditions beyond convergence that should end the session -- populated during initialization]\n56: \n57: ---\n58: \n59: ## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n60: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n61: [None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n62: \n63: | Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n64: |-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n65: | [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n66: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n67: \n68: ---\n69: \n70: ## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n71: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n72: - **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n73: - **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n74: - **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n75: - **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n76: \n77: [Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n78: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n83: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n84: - [Approach]: [Why it worked] (iteration N)\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n89: [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n90: - [Approach]: [Why it failed] (iteration N)\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: ## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n95: [Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n96: \n97: ### [Category Name] -- BLOCKED (iteration N, N attempts)\n98: - What was tried: [specific review approaches attempted]\n99: - Why blocked: [root cause of exhaustion]\n100: - Do NOT retry: [explicit prohibition]\n101: \n102: ### [Category Name] -- PRODUCTIVE (iteration N)\n103: - What worked: [successful review approaches in this category]\n104: - Prefer for: [related dimensions where this category may help]\n105: \n106: ---\n107: \n108: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n109: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n110: - Completed pivots: 0\n111: - Failed pivots: 0\n112: - Audited overrides: 0\n113: - Swept: none yet\n114: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n115: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n116: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n121: [Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n122: - [Approach]: [Why ruled out] (iteration N, evidence: [source])\n123: \n124: ---\n125: \n126: ## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n127: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n128: [Recommended focus area for the next iteration -- updated at end of each iteration. Includes target dimension and/or specific files to review.]\n129: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n130: \n131: ---\n132: \n133: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n134: [Populated during initialization from the continuity ladder and ripgrep recipes, if any prior work exists]\n135: \n136: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n137: \n138: Populate during initialization before the first review dimension runs. Keep this pointer-based and scoped to the declared review target:\n139: \n140: - Target pointers: files, specs, symbols, or resource-map entries under review.\n141: - Behavior claims: acceptance criteria, public contracts, or docs to verify.\n142: - Reuse and conventions: existing patterns that define expected implementation shape.\n143: - Review risks and gaps: stale graph or memory caveats, missing files, and out-of-scope areas.\n144: \n145: Do not inline full source bodies. Do not dispatch the retired standalone context loop. Use this snapshot only to seed review dimensions and final traceability.\n146: \n147: ---\n148: \n149: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n150: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n151: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n152: \n153: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n154: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n155: | `spec_code` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n156: | `checklist_evidence` | core | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked] | [N] | [details] |\n157: | `skill_agent` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n158: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n159: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n160: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | [pending/pass/partial/fail/blocked/notApplicable] | [N] | [details] |\n161: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n162: \n163: ---\n164: \n165: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n166: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n167: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n168: \n169: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n170: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n171: | [path/to/file] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 1 P1, 2 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n172: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n173: \n174: ---\n175: \n176: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n177: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n178: - Max iterations: [from config]\n179: - Convergence threshold: [from config]\n180: - Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n181: - No-progress threshold: 0.05\n182: - Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n183: - Session lineage: sessionId=[from config.sessionId], parentSessionId=[from config.parentSessionId], generation=[from config.generation], lineageMode=[from config.lineageMode]\n184: - Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n185: - Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n186: - Per-iteration budget: [from config.maxToolCallsPerIteration] tool calls, [from config.maxMinutesPerIteration] minutes\n187: - Severity threshold: [from config.severityThreshold]\n188: - Review target type: [from config.reviewTargetType]\n189: - Cross-reference checks: core=[from config.crossReference.core], overlay=[from config.crossReference.overlay]\n190: - Started: [timestamp]\n191: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n192: \n193: ---\n194: \n195: ## 17. EXAMPLE (POPULATED)\n196: \n197: Reference snippet showing a partially populated strategy file mid-review. Use this as a visual anchor when opening a live strategy doc.\n198: \n199: ```markdown\n200: ## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n201: - Target: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research (skill, v1.4.0)\n202: - Dimensions: correctness, test-coverage, cross-runtime-parity, observability\n203: - Stop conditions: rolling newInfoRatio < 0.08 for 2 iterations OR all dimensions converged OR max=7 reached\n204: - Success criteria: zero P0 in correctness; test-coverage P0 resolved or deferred with rationale\n205: \n206: ## 4. NEXT FOCUS\n207: - Dimension: test-coverage\n208: - Files: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs, .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/deep-research-contract-parity.vitest.ts\n209: - Why: Iteration 2 surfaced a P0 (convergence-path coverage gap); needs a focused follow-up before correctness can terminate PASS.\n210: \n211: ## 9. COVERAGE MATRIX\n212: | Dimension            | Status     | Iterations touched |\n213: |----------------------|------------|--------------------|\n214: | correctness          | converged  | 1                  |\n215: | test-coverage        | converging | 2, 4               |\n216: | cross-runtime-parity | converging | 3                  |\n217: | observability        | converging | 4                  |\n218: ```"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760625767,"end":1794760626146}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760626150,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e011ccb7002qHO88gcaJ2MmG3","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e011b9e8001yDh43PVgsD09dy","type":"tool","id":"call_64f33d19d49d47aba0fd5039","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md, lines 1-582\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Format\n3: description: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop, config, JSONL log, strategy, iteration files, and review report.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state format\"\n6:   - \"deep review config schema\"\n7:   - \"review severity weights\"\n8:   - \"file protection levels\"\n9:   - \"review iteration file structure\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.2.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Format\n16: \n17: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: The review packet is reproduced from disk on every resume, so each file's format, mutability, and fields are pinned here for the reducer, the dashboard, the validator, and the resume path.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating deep-review state files emitted by an iteration or by the reducer.\n30: - Implementing a state consumer (e.g. dashboard, advisor probe, downstream packet).\n31: - Debugging JSONL reducer output or auditing schema-version transitions.\n32: - Authoring fixtures that need to round-trip through the reducer.\n33: \n34: The deep review loop uses 9 state files under the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` owned by the target spec:\n35: \n36: | File | Format | Mutability |\n37: |------|--------|------------|\n38: | `deep-review-config.json` | JSON | Immutable after init, except the terminal `status: complete` flip |\n39: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | JSON Lines | Append-only |\n40: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | JSON | Auto-generated reducer state |\n41: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Markdown | Updated each iteration |\n42: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Markdown | Auto-generated (read-only) |\n43: | `.deep-review-pause` | Sentinel | Created/deleted by user |\n44: | `resource-map.md` | Markdown | Emitted once at synthesis unless `resource_map.emit` is false |\n45: | `review-report.md` | Markdown | Updated at synthesis |\n46: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Markdown | Write-once |\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: {artifact_dir}/\n50:   deep-review-config.json\n51:   deep-review-state.jsonl\n52:   deep-review-findings-registry.json\n53:   deep-review-strategy.md\n54:   deep-review-dashboard.md\n55:   .deep-review-pause\n56:   review-report.md\n57:   iterations/\n58:     iteration-001.md\n59:     iteration-002.md\n60:     ...\n61: ```\n62: \n63: `{artifact_dir}` comes from `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')`. Root-spec runs resolve directly to `{spec_folder}/review/`. Child-phase and sub-phase runs use **flat-first**: a first run with an empty `review/` resolves directly to `{spec_folder}/review/` (no `pt-NN` wrapper). A `pt-NN` packet is allocated only when prior content for a non-matching target already exists. Continuation runs reuse the existing flat artifact (or matching `pt-NN` packet). This avoids the unnecessary `pt-01` wrapper on first runs.\n64: \n65: Example (first run on a child phase): `.../026-graph.../006-continuity-refactor-gates/003-gate-c-writer-ready/` → `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/` (flat, no subfolder).\n66: \n67: Example (subsequent run with prior content for a different target): `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/003-gate-c-writer-ready-pt-02/` (`pt-NN` allocated as a sibling to the prior content; subfolder name is `{basename(spec_folder)}-pt-{NN}`).\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 2. CONFIG FILE (deep-review-config.json)\n72: \n73: Created during initialization. Not modified after creation.\n74: \n75: ```json\n76: {\n77:   \"topic\": \"Review of deep-review skill package\",\n78:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n79:   \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n80:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n81:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n82:   \"resource_map_present\": false,\n83:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n84:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n85:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n86:   \"generation\": 1,\n87:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n88:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n89:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n90:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n91:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n92:   \"crossReference\": {\n93:     \"core\": [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"],\n94:     \"overlay\": [\"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n95:   },\n96:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n97:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n98:   \"specFolder\": \"030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n99:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\n100:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n101:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n102:   \"fileProtection\": {\n103:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n104:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n105:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n106:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n107:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n108:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n109:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n110:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n111:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n112:   },\n113:   \"reducer\": {\n114:     \"enabled\": true,\n115:     \"inputs\": [\"latestJSONLDelta\", \"newIterationFile\", \"priorReducedState\"],\n116:     \"outputs\": [\"findingsRegistry\", \"dashboardMetrics\", \"strategyUpdates\"],\n117:     \"metrics\": [\n118:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n119:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n120:       \"openFindings\",\n121:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n122:       \"convergenceScore\"\n123:     ]\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### Field Reference\n129: \n130: | Field | Type | Default | Description |\n131: |-------|------|---------|-------------|\n132: | mode | `\"review\"` | -- | Session mode discriminator (required) |\n133: | reviewTarget | string | -- | Path or identifier of the review target |\n134: | reviewTargetType | string | `\"spec-folder\"` | `spec-folder`, `skill`, `agent`, `track`, `files` |\n135: | reviewDimensions | string[] | all 4 | Dimensions to evaluate |\n136: | resource_map_present | boolean | false | True only when `{specFolder}/resource-map.md` existed during init, enables the Resource Map Coverage audit pass and conditional report section |\n137: | sessionId | string | -- | Stable identifier for the current review lineage |\n138: | parentSessionId | string \\| null | `null` | Parent lineage reference for restart flows |\n139: | lineageMode | string | `\"new\"` | `new`, `resume`, `restart`. `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and not emitted by the current runtime |\n140: | generation | number | 1 | Lineage generation number, incremented on `restart`, unchanged on `resume` |\n141: | continuedFromRun | number \\| null | `null` | Count of completed iteration records at the lifecycle boundary (set on `resume` and `restart`) |\n142: | maxIterations | number | 7 | Hard cap on loop iterations |\n143: | convergenceThreshold | number | 0.10 | Stop when severity-weighted new findings ratio below this |\n144: | stuckThreshold | number | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n145: | severityThreshold | string | `\"P2\"` | Minimum severity to report: `P0`, `P1`, `P2` |\n146: | crossReference | object | -- | Core (hard-gated) and overlay (advisory) protocol sets |\n147: | qualityGateThreshold | boolean | true | Whether binary quality gates are enforced |\n148: | specFolder | string | -- | Spec folder path (relative to specs/) |\n149: | status | string | `\"initialized\"` | `initialized`, `running`, `converged`, `stuck`, `complete`, `error` |\n150: | releaseReadinessState | string | `\"in-progress\"` | `in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking` |\n151: | fileProtection | object | -- | Mutability declarations (see protection levels below) |\n152: | reducer | object | -- | Canonical reducer inputs, outputs, and metrics names |\n153: \n154: ### File Protection Levels\n155: \n156: | Level | Meaning |\n157: |-------|---------|\n158: | immutable | Cannot be modified after creation (config: the terminal `status: complete` flip is the one permitted write) |\n159: | append-only | New content added at end only |\n160: | mutable | Can be read, edited, overwritten |\n161: | write-once | Created once, never modified |\n162: | auto-generated | System-managed, overwritten each refresh |\n163: | operator-controlled | Created or deleted only by the human/operator to control loop state |\n164: \n165: ### Review Dimensions\n166: \n167: | Dimension | Priority | Required for Coverage |\n168: |-----------|----------|---------------------|\n169: | correctness | 1 | Yes |\n170: | security | 2 | Yes |\n171: | traceability | 3 | Yes |\n172: | maintainability | 4 | Yes |\n173: \n174: ### Severity Weights\n175: \n176: | Severity | Weight | Label | Requires file:line |\n177: |----------|--------|-------|--------------------|\n178: | P0 | 10.0 | Blocker | Yes |\n179: | P1 | 5.0 | Required | Yes |\n180: | P2 | 1.0 | Suggestion | Yes |\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 3. STATE LOG\n185: \n186: The `deep-review-state.jsonl` record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema (v2) live in `state-jsonl.md` for navigability.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 4. STRATEGY FILE (deep-review-strategy.md)\n191: \n192: Updated at the end of each iteration. Serves as the persistent brain across fresh-context iterations.\n193: \n194: ### Required Sections\n195: \n196: | Section | Updated By | Purpose |\n197: |---------|-----------|---------|\n198: | topic | Init only | Review topic from config |\n199: | review-dimensions | Each iteration | Unchecked dimensions drive next focus |\n200: | completed-dimensions | Each iteration | Checked dimensions with verdict summary |\n201: | running-findings | Each iteration | P0/P1/P2 active counts + deltas |\n202: | what-worked | Each iteration | Successful approaches for reuse |\n203: | what-failed | Each iteration | Failed approaches to avoid |\n204: | exhausted-approaches | When fully tried | \"Do not retry\" registry |\n205: | ruled-out-directions | Each iteration | Eliminated directions with reasons |\n206: | next-focus | Each iteration | Recommended direction for next iteration |\n207: | known-context | Init only | Prior work from memory context |\n208: | cross-reference-status | Each iteration | Core vs overlay protocol status |\n209: | files-under-review | Each iteration | Per-file coverage state table |\n210: | review-boundaries | Init only | Max iterations, thresholds, config |\n211: \n212: ### Mapping from Research Mode\n213: \n214: | Review Section | Research Equivalent |\n215: |---------------|-------------------|\n216: | review-dimensions | Key Questions (remaining) |\n217: | completed-dimensions | Answered Questions |\n218: | running-findings | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n219: | cross-reference-status | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n220: | files-under-review | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n221: | review-boundaries | Research Boundaries |\n222: \n223: Sections unchanged from research: topic, what-worked, what-failed, exhausted-approaches, ruled-out-directions, next-focus, known-context.\n224: \n225: ### Update Protocol\n226: \n227: 1. Read current strategy file\n228: 2. Move completed dimensions from \"remaining\" to \"completed\" with `[x]` and verdict\n229: 3. Update running-findings with P0/P1/P2 counts and deltas\n230: 4. Add to what-worked / what-failed with iteration number\n231: 5. Move exhausted approaches. Update cross-reference-status and files-under-review\n232: 6. Set next-focus based on remaining dimensions and open findings\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## 5. FINDINGS REGISTRY (deep-review-findings-registry.json)\n237: \n238: Reducer-owned JSON document regenerated after every iteration and lifecycle transition.\n239: \n240: ```json\n241: {\n242:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n243:   \"generation\": 1,\n244:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n245:   \"openFindings\": [],\n246:   \"resolvedFindings\": [],\n247:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n248:   \"persistentSameSeverity\": [],\n249:   \"severityChanged\": [],\n250:   \"repeatedFindings\": [],\n251:   \"dimensionCoverage\": {\n252:     \"correctness\": true,\n253:     \"security\": true,\n254:     \"traceability\": false,\n255:     \"maintainability\": false\n256:   },\n257:   \"findingsBySeverity\": {\n258:     \"P0\": 0,\n259:     \"P1\": 1,\n260:     \"P2\": 2\n261:   },\n262:   \"openFindingsCount\": 3,\n263:   \"resolvedFindingsCount\": 1,\n264:   \"convergenceScore\": 0.44,\n265:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.01,\n266:   \"graphDecision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n267:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n268:   \"corruptionWarnings\": []\n269: }\n270: ```\n271: \n272: This file is machine-owned and must stay synchronized with the latest iteration delta, dashboard metrics, and synthesized review report.\n273: \n274: ### Blocked-Stop and Corruption-Tracking Additions\n275: \n276: | Field | Type | Description |\n277: |-------|------|-------------|\n278: | `blockedStopHistory` | array | One entry per `blocked_stop` JSONL event: `{run, blockedBy, gateResults, recoveryStrategy, timestamp}`. Rendered in the dashboard `BLOCKED STOPS` section and can drive the strategy `next-focus` anchor when blocked-stop is the most recent loop event. |\n279: | `persistentSameSeverity` | array | Findings observed in ≥2 iterations with NO severity transitions beyond initial discovery. REQ-018 split of the deprecated `repeatedFindings` bucket. |\n280: | `severityChanged` | array | Findings that went through at least one severity transition (P0↔P1↔P2) in their `transitions` history. |\n281: | `repeatedFindings` | array | **Deprecated.** Union of `persistentSameSeverity` and `severityChanged`. Retained for backward compatibility, new code should read the split arrays. |\n282: | `corruptionWarnings` | array | Per-line corruption reports from `parseJsonlDetailed()`: `{line, raw, error}`. Non-empty means the reducer detected malformed JSONL. |\n283: \n284: ### Default Values\n285: \n286: When no `graph_convergence` event has been recorded yet, defaults are `graphConvergenceScore: 0`, `graphDecision: null`, and `graphBlockers: []`.\n287: When no `blocked_stop` event has been recorded yet, `blockedStopHistory: []`.\n288: When JSONL parses cleanly, `corruptionWarnings: []`.\n289: \n290: ### Fail-Closed Semantics (REQ-015, REQ-016)\n291: \n292: - **Malformed JSONL**: The reducer CLI exits with code `2` and writes a warning to stderr when `corruptionWarnings.length > 0`. Pass `--lenient` (or `lenient:true` to `reduceReviewState`) to escape-hatch out and preserve the v1.2.0.0 fail-open behavior for legacy packets.\n293: - **Missing machine-owned anchors**: `replaceAnchorSection()` throws `Error('Missing machine-owned anchor \"<id>\" in deep-review strategy file.')` when the strategy file is present but lacks one of the required anchors. Pass `--create-missing-anchors` (or `createMissingAnchors:true`) to bootstrap empty strategy files by appending the missing anchor blocks.\n294: - **Dashboard surfaces**: `CORRUPTION WARNINGS` section lists detected lines. `BLOCKED STOPS` section lists `blockedStopHistory` entries. `GRAPH CONVERGENCE` section reports `graphConvergenceScore` / `graphDecision` / `graphBlockers`.\n295: - **Strategy next-focus override**: When the latest `blocked_stop` event timestamp is newer than the latest iteration timestamp, the reducer rewrites the strategy `next-focus` anchor to surface the blocking gates and recovery hint so operators see the blocker before choosing the next iteration direction.\n296: \n297: ---\n298: \n299: ## 6. ITERATION FILES (review/iterations/iteration-NNN.md)\n300: \n301: Write-once files. One per iteration, zero-padded 3-digit naming.\n302: \n303: ### Structure\n304: \n305: ```markdown\n306: # Iteration [N]: [Focus Area]\n307: \n308: ## Focus\n309: [Dimension(s), files, scope investigated]\n310: \n311: ## Scorecard\n312: - Dimensions covered: [list]\n313: - Files reviewed: [count]\n314: - New findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n315: - Refined findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n316: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n317: \n318: ## Findings\n319: \n320: ### P0, Blocker\n321: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n322: \n323: ### P1, Required\n324: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n325: \n326: ### P2, Suggestion\n327: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n328: \n329: ## Cross-Reference Results\n330: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n331: |----------|--------|------|----------|-------|\n332: | spec_code | pass/partial/fail | hard | file:line | ... |\n333: \n334: ## Assessment\n335: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n336: - Dimensions addressed: [list]\n337: - Novelty justification: [breakdown]\n338: \n339: ## Ruled Out\n340: - [Approach]: [Why], [Evidence]\n341: \n342: ## Dead Ends\n343: - [Direction]: [Why]\n344: \n345: ## Recommended Next Focus\n346: [What to investigate next]\n347: ```\n348: \n349: Every finding must include: unique ID (`F001`...), severity (`P0`/`P1`/`P2`), concrete `file:line` evidence, and dimension tag.\n350: \n351: ---\n352: \n353: ## 7. REVIEW REPORT (review/review-report.md)\n354: \n355: The review synthesis output contains 9 core sections plus a conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present` is true:\n356: \n357: | # | Section | Description |\n358: |---|---------|-------------|\n359: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` flag |\n360: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why result routes to planning or changelog |\n361: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduped active findings with evidence, severity, dimension |\n362: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Ordered lanes grouped by dependency or area |\n363: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec updates implied by findings |\n364: | 6 | Plan Seed | Initial remediation tasks from findings |\n365: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol outcomes and gaps |\n366: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` existed at init, contains touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n367: | 9 | Deferred Items | Advisory findings, blocked items, follow-up checks |\n368: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, convergence replay, audit detail |\n369: \n370: **Executive Summary** includes verdict (`PASS`/`CONDITIONAL`/`FAIL`), active finding counts, `hasAdvisories` boolean (PASS + P2 > 0), scope description, and convergence reason.\n371: \n372: **Planning Trigger** routes FAIL/CONDITIONAL to remediation planning, PASS to changelog creation.\n373: \n374: **Active Finding Registry** lists each active finding with findingId, severity, dimension, title, file:line evidence, first/last seen iteration, and status.\n375: \n376: **Remediation Workstreams** group related findings into ordered lanes with constituent finding IDs and execution order.\n377: \n378: **Spec Seed / Plan Seed** provide minimal spec updates and initial remediation tasks referencing finding IDs and target files.\n379: \n380: **Traceability Status** reports per-protocol pass/partial/fail with gating class and evidence.\n381: \n382: **Resource Map Coverage Gate** is emitted only when `resource_map_present` is true and MUST contain exactly three bullets: touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map.\n383: \n384: **Deferred Items** captures advisory findings, blocked protocols, and future follow-up checks.\n385: \n386: **Audit Appendix** contains iteration table, convergence signal replay, file coverage matrix, and dimension breakdown.\n387: \n388: ---\n389: \n390: ## 8. DASHBOARD (review/deep-review-dashboard.md)\n391: \n392: Auto-generated summary. Never manually edited.\n393: \n394: - **Path**: `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n395: - **Generated from**: JSONL state log + strategy + findings registry\n396: - **Refresh**: Regenerated after every iteration\n397: - **Protection**: `auto-generated` in fileProtection\n398: \n399: ### Sections\n400: \n401: | Section | Source | Description |\n402: |---------|--------|-------------|\n403: | Findings Summary | JSONL | Active P0/P1/P2 counts, new vs refined |\n404: | Progress Table | JSONL | Run, status, focus, dimensions, ratio, duration |\n405: | Coverage | Strategy + JSONL | Dimension completion, file coverage, protocol status |\n406: | Trend | JSONL signals | Rolling average, composite stop score, trajectory |\n407: \n408: **Rules:** Sole inputs are JSONL + strategy. Overwrite entirely on refresh. Read-only for all agents.\n409: \n410: ---\n411: \n412: ## 9. CLAIM ADJUDICATION\n413: \n414: Every new P0/P1 finding must carry a **typed claim-adjudication packet**. The packet is parsed by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication` in the review workflow and its pass/fail result is persisted as a `claim_adjudication` event in `deep-review-state.jsonl`. The next iteration's `step_check_convergence` legal-stop decision tree reads the latest event via `claimAdjudicationGate` (gate `f`), a missing or failed packet vetoes STOP even if every other gate passes. Prose-only adjudication blocks are no longer accepted.\n415: \n416: The persisted gate result is the flat `claim_adjudication` event, and it is canonical in its own right. The ledger registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication` for exactly this run-level summary and separately registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication_recorded` for the typed per-finding record (`findingId`, `claimDigest`, `finalSeverity`, `adjudicationOutcome`). They are not aliases: the payloads are closed and disjoint, so a producer holding only gate counts writes the flat stem and never invents the typed fields. Section 11 lists the registered vocabulary and the check that holds it to the emitter surface on disk.\n417: \n418: ### Typed Packet Schema (required)\n419: \n420: Embed the packet inside the iteration file for each new P0/P1 finding. The orchestrator parses it after evaluation and persists the validation result.\n421: \n422: ```json\n423: {\n424:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n425:   \"claim\": \"Coverage-graph upsert identity is bare `id`, so cross-session collisions overwrite prior rows.\",\n426:   \"evidenceRefs\": [\n427:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:154\",\n428:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:292-302\"\n429:   ],\n430:   \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Grepped the module for compound-key upserts, checked migration scripts, and inspected the composite-key upserts in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` for a collision regression, none found.\",\n431:   \"alternativeExplanation\": \"Could be intentional single-tenant design, but REQ-024 explicitly requires session isolation, so this is rejected.\",\n432:   \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n433:   \"confidence\": 0.86,\n434:   \"downgradeTrigger\": \"If a composite primary key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` lands and a collision regression covers the ID-reuse path, downgrade to P2 tech-debt.\",\n435:   \"transitions\": [\n436:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" }\n437:   ]\n438: }\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Required Fields\n442: \n443: | Field | Type | Description |\n444: |-------|------|-------------|\n445: | `findingId` | string | Must match the finding ID in the iteration body and registry |\n446: | `claim` | string | The single assertion the finding makes (one sentence, evidence-backed) |\n447: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | `file:line` or `file:range` citations that substantiate the claim (at least one entry) |\n448: | `counterevidenceSought` | string | Where the reviewer looked for contradicting evidence (commands, paths, docs), blank string is not acceptable |\n449: | `alternativeExplanation` | string | An alternative reading of the evidence, even if the reviewer rejects it |\n450: | `finalSeverity` | `\"P0\"` \\| `\"P1\"` \\| `\"P2\"` | Severity after adjudication (may differ from the severity originally asserted) |\n451: | `confidence` | number `[0, 1]` | Reviewer confidence in `finalSeverity` |\n452: | `downgradeTrigger` | string | The concrete condition under which this finding should be downgraded in a future iteration |\n453: | `transitions` | object[] | Optional severity transition log, required when `finalSeverity` differs from the originally asserted severity |\n454: \n455: ### Validation Rules (enforced by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication`)\n456: \n457: 1. A packet MUST exist for every new P0/P1 finding introduced in this iteration. Carried-forward findings reuse the previous packet unless severity transitioned.\n458: 2. All required fields MUST be present and non-empty. `confidence` MUST be a number in `[0, 1]`.\n459: 3. Each `evidenceRefs` entry MUST contain a `:` separating the path from a line or range.\n460: 4. `finalSeverity` MUST match the severity the finding is registered under in the iteration's `Findings` section and in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n461: 5. When any rule fails, the workflow appends `{\"event\":\"claim_adjudication\",\"passed\":false,\"missingPackets\":[...]}` to the state log. The next `step_check_convergence` call reads that event and sets `claimAdjudicationGate` = `false`, producing a `blockedStop` event with `blockedBy: [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]` until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packet.\n462: \n463: ### Severity Transition Rules\n464: \n465: - **P2 → P1**: confirmed exploitable impact or spec violation with direct evidence\n466: - **P1 → P0**: demonstrated data loss, security breach, or hard-gate failure\n467: - **Downgrade**: requires explicit counterevidence or a confirmed alternative explanation\n468: - Every transition is recorded in the packet's `transitions` array and mirrored into the finding registry's `transitions` field\n469: \n470: ---\n471: \n472: ## 10. FINDING REGISTRY\n473: \n474: Each finding is tracked with a unique identifier enabling deduplication, severity transitions, and status lifecycle.\n475: \n476: ### Schema\n477: \n478: ```json\n479: {\n480:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n481:   \"severity\": \"P1\",\n482:   \"category\": \"resource-map-coverage\",\n483:   \"status\": \"active\",\n484:   \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n485:   \"title\": \"Applied target file missing from resource-map inventory\",\n486:   \"file\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\",\n487:   \"line\": 955,\n488:   \"firstSeen\": 2,\n489:   \"lastSeen\": 4,\n490:   \"transitions\": [\n491:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" },\n492:     { \"iteration\": 4, \"from\": \"P2\", \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Confirmed real coverage gap against applied target inventory\" }\n493:   ]\n494: }\n495: ```\n496: \n497: | Field | Type | Description |\n498: |-------|------|-------------|\n499: | findingId | string | Sequential unique ID: `F001`, `F002`, ... |\n500: | severity | `\"P0\"` / `\"P1\"` / `\"P2\"` | Current severity |\n501: | category | `\"correctness\"` / `\"security\"` / `\"traceability\"` / `\"maintainability\"` / `\"resource-map-coverage\"` | Primary audit category for the finding, `resource-map-coverage` is reserved for implementation-vs-map coverage gaps |\n502: | status | `\"active\"` / `\"resolved\"` / `\"deferred\"` / `\"disproved\"` | Current status |\n503: | dimension | string | Primary dimension: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability |\n504: | title | string | Short description |\n505: | file | string | File path |\n506: | line | number | Line number (approximate) |\n507: | firstSeen / lastSeen | number | Iteration where first discovered / last referenced |\n508: | transitions | array | Severity and status change history |\n509: \n510: ### Status Lifecycle\n511: \n512: ```text\n513: [discovered] --> active --> resolved    (fixed or confirmed non-issue)\n514:                   |\n515:                   +--> deferred    (advisory, below threshold)\n516:                   |\n517:                   +--> disproved   (counterevidence invalidated)\n518: ```\n519: \n520: | Status | Counts Toward Verdict |\n521: |--------|----------------------|\n522: | active | Yes |\n523: | resolved | No |\n524: | deferred | No (listed in Deferred Items) |\n525: | disproved | No |\n526: \n527: ### Deduplication\n528: \n529: Same file + line range + root cause as an existing finding = **refinement**, not new. The existing findingId is updated. Refinements count at half weight (`refinementMultiplier: 0.5`) and are tracked via `findingsRefined` in JSONL.\n530: \n531: ### Cross-Reference Protocols\n532: \n533: | Protocol | Level | Applies To | Gate |\n534: |----------|-------|------------|------|\n535: | spec_code | core | all types | hard |\n536: | checklist_evidence | core | all types | hard |\n537: | skill_agent | overlay | skill | advisory |\n538: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | agent | advisory |\n539: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | skill, spec-folder, track, files | advisory |\n540: | playbook_capability | overlay | skill, agent, spec-folder | advisory |\n541: \n542: Severity for `resource-map-coverage` findings is calibrated to the coverage-gate outcome:\n543: - `P2` when an untouched map entry is explicitly `expected-by-scope`\n544: - `P1` when an untouched or absent path represents a real coverage gap\n545: - `P0` only when the missing coverage masks a release-blocking correctness or security risk\n546: \n547: ### Quality Gates\n548: \n549: | Gate | Rule |\n550: |------|------|\n551: | Evidence | Every active finding backed by concrete file:line evidence |\n552: | Scope | Reviewed files and conclusions stay inside declared scope |\n553: | Coverage | Required dimensions and required protocols covered |\n554: \n555: All three gates must pass before STOP. Gate failure forces `verdict: \"FAIL\"` regardless of finding counts.\n556: \n557: ---\n558: \n559: ## 11. LEDGER VOCABULARY AND PROJECTION CEILING\n560: \n561: ### Registered vocabulary\n562: \n563: The canonical dotted stems for this mode live in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts`:\n564: \n565: - `DeepReviewEventStems` — the registered stems the ledger accepts.\n566: - `DEEP_REVIEW_STEM_PRODUCERS` — one entry per stem recording whether a mechanical producer emits it today (`spoken`, with the producer files) or why nothing does (`reserved`).\n567: \n568: The registry is only honest while it matches the emitter surface. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs` scans the workflow assets and runtime scripts and fails (exit 2) when a registered stem has no producer, a spoken stem has no emitter, or a reserved stem is emitted anyway:\n569: \n570: ```bash\n571: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs\n572: ```\n573: \n574: ### Which file is authoritative\n575: \n576: `deep-review-state.jsonl` is authoritative while the mode's authority record (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`) names the legacy writer. Once the record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger is authoritative and this file becomes a projection that the append gateway refreshes after each append.\n577: \n578: ### What a projection refresh can reproduce\n579: \n580: The projection folds only registered stems, and its `run_initialized` arm rebuilds a thin config row: `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, `timestamp`. A pre-flip config row written by the workflow carries attribution the fold cannot rebuild — `mode`, `reviewTarget`, `reviewTargetType`, `reviewDimensions`, `resource_map_present`, `resource_map`, `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence`, `stopPolicy`, `executor`, `createdAt`, `specFolder`.\n581: \n582: Because losing those keys silently would make the projection look complete while the operator's context is gone, a replace that would drop keys from an existing `type: \"config\"` first row is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` (invariant `no-attribution-loss-on-replace`) before any bytes are written. An operator who hits it either migrates the attribution into a registered `deep_review.run_initialized` payload or intentionally moves the legacy file aside to accept the loss.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md, lines 1-582\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Review State Format\n3: description: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop, config, JSONL log, strategy, iteration files, and review report.\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"deep review state format\"\n6:   - \"deep review config schema\"\n7:   - \"review severity weights\"\n8:   - \"file protection levels\"\n9:   - \"review iteration file structure\"\n10: importance_tier: important\n11: contextType: implementation\n12: version: 1.11.2.0\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # Deep Review State Format\n16: \n17: State file schemas for the autonomous deep review loop.\n18: \n19: ---\n20: \n21: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n22: \n23: ### Purpose\n24: \n25: The review packet is reproduced from disk on every resume, so each file's format, mutability, and fields are pinned here for the reducer, the dashboard, the validator, and the resume path.\n26: \n27: ### When to Use\n28: \n29: - Validating deep-review state files emitted by an iteration or by the reducer.\n30: - Implementing a state consumer (e.g. dashboard, advisor probe, downstream packet).\n31: - Debugging JSONL reducer output or auditing schema-version transitions.\n32: - Authoring fixtures that need to round-trip through the reducer.\n33: \n34: The deep review loop uses 9 state files under the resolved `{artifact_dir}/` owned by the target spec:\n35: \n36: | File | Format | Mutability |\n37: |------|--------|------------|\n38: | `deep-review-config.json` | JSON | Immutable after init, except the terminal `status: complete` flip |\n39: | `deep-review-state.jsonl` | JSON Lines | Append-only |\n40: | `deep-review-findings-registry.json` | JSON | Auto-generated reducer state |\n41: | `deep-review-strategy.md` | Markdown | Updated each iteration |\n42: | `deep-review-dashboard.md` | Markdown | Auto-generated (read-only) |\n43: | `.deep-review-pause` | Sentinel | Created/deleted by user |\n44: | `resource-map.md` | Markdown | Emitted once at synthesis unless `resource_map.emit` is false |\n45: | `review-report.md` | Markdown | Updated at synthesis |\n46: | `iterations/iteration-NNN.md` | Markdown | Write-once |\n47: \n48: ```text\n49: {artifact_dir}/\n50:   deep-review-config.json\n51:   deep-review-state.jsonl\n52:   deep-review-findings-registry.json\n53:   deep-review-strategy.md\n54:   deep-review-dashboard.md\n55:   .deep-review-pause\n56:   review-report.md\n57:   iterations/\n58:     iteration-001.md\n59:     iteration-002.md\n60:     ...\n61: ```\n62: \n63: `{artifact_dir}` comes from `resolveArtifactRoot(specFolder, 'review')`. Root-spec runs resolve directly to `{spec_folder}/review/`. Child-phase and sub-phase runs use **flat-first**: a first run with an empty `review/` resolves directly to `{spec_folder}/review/` (no `pt-NN` wrapper). A `pt-NN` packet is allocated only when prior content for a non-matching target already exists. Continuation runs reuse the existing flat artifact (or matching `pt-NN` packet). This avoids the unnecessary `pt-01` wrapper on first runs.\n64: \n65: Example (first run on a child phase): `.../026-graph.../006-continuity-refactor-gates/003-gate-c-writer-ready/` → `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/` (flat, no subfolder).\n66: \n67: Example (subsequent run with prior content for a different target): `003-gate-c-writer-ready/review/003-gate-c-writer-ready-pt-02/` (`pt-NN` allocated as a sibling to the prior content; subfolder name is `{basename(spec_folder)}-pt-{NN}`).\n68: \n69: ---\n70: \n71: ## 2. CONFIG FILE (deep-review-config.json)\n72: \n73: Created during initialization. Not modified after creation.\n74: \n75: ```json\n76: {\n77:   \"topic\": \"Review of deep-review skill package\",\n78:   \"mode\": \"review\",\n79:   \"reviewTarget\": \"specs/030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n80:   \"reviewTargetType\": \"spec-folder\",\n81:   \"reviewDimensions\": [\"correctness\", \"security\", \"traceability\", \"maintainability\"],\n82:   \"resource_map_present\": false,\n83:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n84:   \"parentSessionId\": null,\n85:   \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n86:   \"generation\": 1,\n87:   \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n88:   \"maxIterations\": 7,\n89:   \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.10,\n90:   \"stuckThreshold\": 2,\n91:   \"severityThreshold\": \"P2\",\n92:   \"crossReference\": {\n93:     \"core\": [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"],\n94:     \"overlay\": [\"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n95:   },\n96:   \"qualityGateThreshold\": true,\n97:   \"releaseReadinessState\": \"in-progress\",\n98:   \"specFolder\": \"030-deep-review-review-mode\",\n99:   \"createdAt\": \"2026-03-24T14:00:00Z\",\n100:   \"status\": \"initialized\",\n101:   \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n102:   \"fileProtection\": {\n103:     \"deep-review-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n104:     \"deep-review-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n105:     \"deep-review-findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n106:     \"deep-review-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n107:     \"deep-review-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n108:     \".deep-review-pause\": \"operator-controlled\",\n109:     \"review-report.md\": \"mutable\",\n110:     \"review-report-v*.md\": \"write-once\",\n111:     \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\"\n112:   },\n113:   \"reducer\": {\n114:     \"enabled\": true,\n115:     \"inputs\": [\"latestJSONLDelta\", \"newIterationFile\", \"priorReducedState\"],\n116:     \"outputs\": [\"findingsRegistry\", \"dashboardMetrics\", \"strategyUpdates\"],\n117:     \"metrics\": [\n118:       \"dimensionsCovered\",\n119:       \"findingsBySeverity\",\n120:       \"openFindings\",\n121:       \"resolvedFindings\",\n122:       \"convergenceScore\"\n123:     ]\n124:   }\n125: }\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ### Field Reference\n129: \n130: | Field | Type | Default | Description |\n131: |-------|------|---------|-------------|\n132: | mode | `\"review\"` | -- | Session mode discriminator (required) |\n133: | reviewTarget | string | -- | Path or identifier of the review target |\n134: | reviewTargetType | string | `\"spec-folder\"` | `spec-folder`, `skill`, `agent`, `track`, `files` |\n135: | reviewDimensions | string[] | all 4 | Dimensions to evaluate |\n136: | resource_map_present | boolean | false | True only when `{specFolder}/resource-map.md` existed during init, enables the Resource Map Coverage audit pass and conditional report section |\n137: | sessionId | string | -- | Stable identifier for the current review lineage |\n138: | parentSessionId | string \\| null | `null` | Parent lineage reference for restart flows |\n139: | lineageMode | string | `\"new\"` | `new`, `resume`, `restart`. `fork` and `completed-continue` are deferred and not emitted by the current runtime |\n140: | generation | number | 1 | Lineage generation number, incremented on `restart`, unchanged on `resume` |\n141: | continuedFromRun | number \\| null | `null` | Count of completed iteration records at the lifecycle boundary (set on `resume` and `restart`) |\n142: | maxIterations | number | 7 | Hard cap on loop iterations |\n143: | convergenceThreshold | number | 0.10 | Stop when severity-weighted new findings ratio below this |\n144: | stuckThreshold | number | 2 | Consecutive no-progress iterations before recovery |\n145: | severityThreshold | string | `\"P2\"` | Minimum severity to report: `P0`, `P1`, `P2` |\n146: | crossReference | object | -- | Core (hard-gated) and overlay (advisory) protocol sets |\n147: | qualityGateThreshold | boolean | true | Whether binary quality gates are enforced |\n148: | specFolder | string | -- | Spec folder path (relative to specs/) |\n149: | status | string | `\"initialized\"` | `initialized`, `running`, `converged`, `stuck`, `complete`, `error` |\n150: | releaseReadinessState | string | `\"in-progress\"` | `in-progress`, `converged`, `release-blocking` |\n151: | fileProtection | object | -- | Mutability declarations (see protection levels below) |\n152: | reducer | object | -- | Canonical reducer inputs, outputs, and metrics names |\n153: \n154: ### File Protection Levels\n155: \n156: | Level | Meaning |\n157: |-------|---------|\n158: | immutable | Cannot be modified after creation (config: the terminal `status: complete` flip is the one permitted write) |\n159: | append-only | New content added at end only |\n160: | mutable | Can be read, edited, overwritten |\n161: | write-once | Created once, never modified |\n162: | auto-generated | System-managed, overwritten each refresh |\n163: | operator-controlled | Created or deleted only by the human/operator to control loop state |\n164: \n165: ### Review Dimensions\n166: \n167: | Dimension | Priority | Required for Coverage |\n168: |-----------|----------|---------------------|\n169: | correctness | 1 | Yes |\n170: | security | 2 | Yes |\n171: | traceability | 3 | Yes |\n172: | maintainability | 4 | Yes |\n173: \n174: ### Severity Weights\n175: \n176: | Severity | Weight | Label | Requires file:line |\n177: |----------|--------|-------|--------------------|\n178: | P0 | 10.0 | Blocker | Yes |\n179: | P1 | 5.0 | Required | Yes |\n180: | P2 | 1.0 | Suggestion | Yes |\n181: \n182: ---\n183: \n184: ## 3. STATE LOG\n185: \n186: The `deep-review-state.jsonl` record schemas (config, iteration, event, lineage) and the Review Depth Schema (v2) live in `state-jsonl.md` for navigability.\n187: \n188: ---\n189: \n190: ## 4. STRATEGY FILE (deep-review-strategy.md)\n191: \n192: Updated at the end of each iteration. Serves as the persistent brain across fresh-context iterations.\n193: \n194: ### Required Sections\n195: \n196: | Section | Updated By | Purpose |\n197: |---------|-----------|---------|\n198: | topic | Init only | Review topic from config |\n199: | review-dimensions | Each iteration | Unchecked dimensions drive next focus |\n200: | completed-dimensions | Each iteration | Checked dimensions with verdict summary |\n201: | running-findings | Each iteration | P0/P1/P2 active counts + deltas |\n202: | what-worked | Each iteration | Successful approaches for reuse |\n203: | what-failed | Each iteration | Failed approaches to avoid |\n204: | exhausted-approaches | When fully tried | \"Do not retry\" registry |\n205: | ruled-out-directions | Each iteration | Eliminated directions with reasons |\n206: | next-focus | Each iteration | Recommended direction for next iteration |\n207: | known-context | Init only | Prior work from memory context |\n208: | cross-reference-status | Each iteration | Core vs overlay protocol status |\n209: | files-under-review | Each iteration | Per-file coverage state table |\n210: | review-boundaries | Init only | Max iterations, thresholds, config |\n211: \n212: ### Mapping from Research Mode\n213: \n214: | Review Section | Research Equivalent |\n215: |---------------|-------------------|\n216: | review-dimensions | Key Questions (remaining) |\n217: | completed-dimensions | Answered Questions |\n218: | running-findings | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n219: | cross-reference-status | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n220: | files-under-review | _(none, review-specific)_ |\n221: | review-boundaries | Research Boundaries |\n222: \n223: Sections unchanged from research: topic, what-worked, what-failed, exhausted-approaches, ruled-out-directions, next-focus, known-context.\n224: \n225: ### Update Protocol\n226: \n227: 1. Read current strategy file\n228: 2. Move completed dimensions from \"remaining\" to \"completed\" with `[x]` and verdict\n229: 3. Update running-findings with P0/P1/P2 counts and deltas\n230: 4. Add to what-worked / what-failed with iteration number\n231: 5. Move exhausted approaches. Update cross-reference-status and files-under-review\n232: 6. Set next-focus based on remaining dimensions and open findings\n233: \n234: ---\n235: \n236: ## 5. FINDINGS REGISTRY (deep-review-findings-registry.json)\n237: \n238: Reducer-owned JSON document regenerated after every iteration and lifecycle transition.\n239: \n240: ```json\n241: {\n242:   \"sessionId\": \"rvw-2026-04-03T12-00-00Z\",\n243:   \"generation\": 1,\n244:   \"lineageMode\": \"resume\",\n245:   \"openFindings\": [],\n246:   \"resolvedFindings\": [],\n247:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n248:   \"persistentSameSeverity\": [],\n249:   \"severityChanged\": [],\n250:   \"repeatedFindings\": [],\n251:   \"dimensionCoverage\": {\n252:     \"correctness\": true,\n253:     \"security\": true,\n254:     \"traceability\": false,\n255:     \"maintainability\": false\n256:   },\n257:   \"findingsBySeverity\": {\n258:     \"P0\": 0,\n259:     \"P1\": 1,\n260:     \"P2\": 2\n261:   },\n262:   \"openFindingsCount\": 3,\n263:   \"resolvedFindingsCount\": 1,\n264:   \"convergenceScore\": 0.44,\n265:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.01,\n266:   \"graphDecision\": \"STOP_ALLOWED\",\n267:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n268:   \"corruptionWarnings\": []\n269: }\n270: ```\n271: \n272: This file is machine-owned and must stay synchronized with the latest iteration delta, dashboard metrics, and synthesized review report.\n273: \n274: ### Blocked-Stop and Corruption-Tracking Additions\n275: \n276: | Field | Type | Description |\n277: |-------|------|-------------|\n278: | `blockedStopHistory` | array | One entry per `blocked_stop` JSONL event: `{run, blockedBy, gateResults, recoveryStrategy, timestamp}`. Rendered in the dashboard `BLOCKED STOPS` section and can drive the strategy `next-focus` anchor when blocked-stop is the most recent loop event. |\n279: | `persistentSameSeverity` | array | Findings observed in ≥2 iterations with NO severity transitions beyond initial discovery. REQ-018 split of the deprecated `repeatedFindings` bucket. |\n280: | `severityChanged` | array | Findings that went through at least one severity transition (P0↔P1↔P2) in their `transitions` history. |\n281: | `repeatedFindings` | array | **Deprecated.** Union of `persistentSameSeverity` and `severityChanged`. Retained for backward compatibility, new code should read the split arrays. |\n282: | `corruptionWarnings` | array | Per-line corruption reports from `parseJsonlDetailed()`: `{line, raw, error}`. Non-empty means the reducer detected malformed JSONL. |\n283: \n284: ### Default Values\n285: \n286: When no `graph_convergence` event has been recorded yet, defaults are `graphConvergenceScore: 0`, `graphDecision: null`, and `graphBlockers: []`.\n287: When no `blocked_stop` event has been recorded yet, `blockedStopHistory: []`.\n288: When JSONL parses cleanly, `corruptionWarnings: []`.\n289: \n290: ### Fail-Closed Semantics (REQ-015, REQ-016)\n291: \n292: - **Malformed JSONL**: The reducer CLI exits with code `2` and writes a warning to stderr when `corruptionWarnings.length > 0`. Pass `--lenient` (or `lenient:true` to `reduceReviewState`) to escape-hatch out and preserve the v1.2.0.0 fail-open behavior for legacy packets.\n293: - **Missing machine-owned anchors**: `replaceAnchorSection()` throws `Error('Missing machine-owned anchor \"<id>\" in deep-review strategy file.')` when the strategy file is present but lacks one of the required anchors. Pass `--create-missing-anchors` (or `createMissingAnchors:true`) to bootstrap empty strategy files by appending the missing anchor blocks.\n294: - **Dashboard surfaces**: `CORRUPTION WARNINGS` section lists detected lines. `BLOCKED STOPS` section lists `blockedStopHistory` entries. `GRAPH CONVERGENCE` section reports `graphConvergenceScore` / `graphDecision` / `graphBlockers`.\n295: - **Strategy next-focus override**: When the latest `blocked_stop` event timestamp is newer than the latest iteration timestamp, the reducer rewrites the strategy `next-focus` anchor to surface the blocking gates and recovery hint so operators see the blocker before choosing the next iteration direction.\n296: \n297: ---\n298: \n299: ## 6. ITERATION FILES (review/iterations/iteration-NNN.md)\n300: \n301: Write-once files. One per iteration, zero-padded 3-digit naming.\n302: \n303: ### Structure\n304: \n305: ```markdown\n306: # Iteration [N]: [Focus Area]\n307: \n308: ## Focus\n309: [Dimension(s), files, scope investigated]\n310: \n311: ## Scorecard\n312: - Dimensions covered: [list]\n313: - Files reviewed: [count]\n314: - New findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n315: - Refined findings: P0=[n] P1=[n] P2=[n]\n316: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n317: \n318: ## Findings\n319: \n320: ### P0, Blocker\n321: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n322: \n323: ### P1, Required\n324: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n325: \n326: ### P2, Suggestion\n327: - **F[NNN]**: [Title], `file:line`, [Description with evidence]\n328: \n329: ## Cross-Reference Results\n330: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n331: |----------|--------|------|----------|-------|\n332: | spec_code | pass/partial/fail | hard | file:line | ... |\n333: \n334: ## Assessment\n335: - New findings ratio: [0.0-1.0]\n336: - Dimensions addressed: [list]\n337: - Novelty justification: [breakdown]\n338: \n339: ## Ruled Out\n340: - [Approach]: [Why], [Evidence]\n341: \n342: ## Dead Ends\n343: - [Direction]: [Why]\n344: \n345: ## Recommended Next Focus\n346: [What to investigate next]\n347: ```\n348: \n349: Every finding must include: unique ID (`F001`...), severity (`P0`/`P1`/`P2`), concrete `file:line` evidence, and dimension tag.\n350: \n351: ---\n352: \n353: ## 7. REVIEW REPORT (review/review-report.md)\n354: \n355: The review synthesis output contains 9 core sections plus a conditional `## Resource Map Coverage Gate` section when `resource_map_present` is true:\n356: \n357: | # | Section | Description |\n358: |---|---------|-------------|\n359: | 1 | Executive Summary | Verdict, active P0/P1/P2 counts, scope, `hasAdvisories` flag |\n360: | 2 | Planning Trigger | Why result routes to planning or changelog |\n361: | 3 | Active Finding Registry | Deduped active findings with evidence, severity, dimension |\n362: | 4 | Remediation Workstreams | Ordered lanes grouped by dependency or area |\n363: | 5 | Spec Seed | Minimal spec updates implied by findings |\n364: | 6 | Plan Seed | Initial remediation tasks from findings |\n365: | 7 | Traceability Status | Core vs overlay protocol outcomes and gaps |\n366: | 8 | Resource Map Coverage Gate | Present only when `{spec_folder}/resource-map.md` existed at init, contains touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map |\n367: | 9 | Deferred Items | Advisory findings, blocked items, follow-up checks |\n368: | 10 | Audit Appendix | Coverage, convergence replay, audit detail |\n369: \n370: **Executive Summary** includes verdict (`PASS`/`CONDITIONAL`/`FAIL`), active finding counts, `hasAdvisories` boolean (PASS + P2 > 0), scope description, and convergence reason.\n371: \n372: **Planning Trigger** routes FAIL/CONDITIONAL to remediation planning, PASS to changelog creation.\n373: \n374: **Active Finding Registry** lists each active finding with findingId, severity, dimension, title, file:line evidence, first/last seen iteration, and status.\n375: \n376: **Remediation Workstreams** group related findings into ordered lanes with constituent finding IDs and execution order.\n377: \n378: **Spec Seed / Plan Seed** provide minimal spec updates and initial remediation tasks referencing finding IDs and target files.\n379: \n380: **Traceability Status** reports per-protocol pass/partial/fail with gating class and evidence.\n381: \n382: **Resource Map Coverage Gate** is emitted only when `resource_map_present` is true and MUST contain exactly three bullets: touched entries, untouched entries (`expected-by-scope` vs `gap`), and implementation paths absent from the map.\n383: \n384: **Deferred Items** captures advisory findings, blocked protocols, and future follow-up checks.\n385: \n386: **Audit Appendix** contains iteration table, convergence signal replay, file coverage matrix, and dimension breakdown.\n387: \n388: ---\n389: \n390: ## 8. DASHBOARD (review/deep-review-dashboard.md)\n391: \n392: Auto-generated summary. Never manually edited.\n393: \n394: - **Path**: `{artifact_dir}/deep-review-dashboard.md`\n395: - **Generated from**: JSONL state log + strategy + findings registry\n396: - **Refresh**: Regenerated after every iteration\n397: - **Protection**: `auto-generated` in fileProtection\n398: \n399: ### Sections\n400: \n401: | Section | Source | Description |\n402: |---------|--------|-------------|\n403: | Findings Summary | JSONL | Active P0/P1/P2 counts, new vs refined |\n404: | Progress Table | JSONL | Run, status, focus, dimensions, ratio, duration |\n405: | Coverage | Strategy + JSONL | Dimension completion, file coverage, protocol status |\n406: | Trend | JSONL signals | Rolling average, composite stop score, trajectory |\n407: \n408: **Rules:** Sole inputs are JSONL + strategy. Overwrite entirely on refresh. Read-only for all agents.\n409: \n410: ---\n411: \n412: ## 9. CLAIM ADJUDICATION\n413: \n414: Every new P0/P1 finding must carry a **typed claim-adjudication packet**. The packet is parsed by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication` in the review workflow and its pass/fail result is persisted as a `claim_adjudication` event in `deep-review-state.jsonl`. The next iteration's `step_check_convergence` legal-stop decision tree reads the latest event via `claimAdjudicationGate` (gate `f`), a missing or failed packet vetoes STOP even if every other gate passes. Prose-only adjudication blocks are no longer accepted.\n415: \n416: The persisted gate result is the flat `claim_adjudication` event, and it is canonical in its own right. The ledger registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication` for exactly this run-level summary and separately registers `deep_review.claim_adjudication_recorded` for the typed per-finding record (`findingId`, `claimDigest`, `finalSeverity`, `adjudicationOutcome`). They are not aliases: the payloads are closed and disjoint, so a producer holding only gate counts writes the flat stem and never invents the typed fields. Section 11 lists the registered vocabulary and the check that holds it to the emitter surface on disk.\n417: \n418: ### Typed Packet Schema (required)\n419: \n420: Embed the packet inside the iteration file for each new P0/P1 finding. The orchestrator parses it after evaluation and persists the validation result.\n421: \n422: ```json\n423: {\n424:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n425:   \"claim\": \"Coverage-graph upsert identity is bare `id`, so cross-session collisions overwrite prior rows.\",\n426:   \"evidenceRefs\": [\n427:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:154\",\n428:     \".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts:292-302\"\n429:   ],\n430:   \"counterevidenceSought\": \"Grepped the module for compound-key upserts, checked migration scripts, and inspected the composite-key upserts in `runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-db.ts` for a collision regression, none found.\",\n431:   \"alternativeExplanation\": \"Could be intentional single-tenant design, but REQ-024 explicitly requires session isolation, so this is rejected.\",\n432:   \"finalSeverity\": \"P1\",\n433:   \"confidence\": 0.86,\n434:   \"downgradeTrigger\": \"If a composite primary key `(spec_folder, loop_type, session_id, id)` lands and a collision regression covers the ID-reuse path, downgrade to P2 tech-debt.\",\n435:   \"transitions\": [\n436:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" }\n437:   ]\n438: }\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Required Fields\n442: \n443: | Field | Type | Description |\n444: |-------|------|-------------|\n445: | `findingId` | string | Must match the finding ID in the iteration body and registry |\n446: | `claim` | string | The single assertion the finding makes (one sentence, evidence-backed) |\n447: | `evidenceRefs` | string[] | `file:line` or `file:range` citations that substantiate the claim (at least one entry) |\n448: | `counterevidenceSought` | string | Where the reviewer looked for contradicting evidence (commands, paths, docs), blank string is not acceptable |\n449: | `alternativeExplanation` | string | An alternative reading of the evidence, even if the reviewer rejects it |\n450: | `finalSeverity` | `\"P0\"` \\| `\"P1\"` \\| `\"P2\"` | Severity after adjudication (may differ from the severity originally asserted) |\n451: | `confidence` | number `[0, 1]` | Reviewer confidence in `finalSeverity` |\n452: | `downgradeTrigger` | string | The concrete condition under which this finding should be downgraded in a future iteration |\n453: | `transitions` | object[] | Optional severity transition log, required when `finalSeverity` differs from the originally asserted severity |\n454: \n455: ### Validation Rules (enforced by `step_post_iteration_claim_adjudication`)\n456: \n457: 1. A packet MUST exist for every new P0/P1 finding introduced in this iteration. Carried-forward findings reuse the previous packet unless severity transitioned.\n458: 2. All required fields MUST be present and non-empty. `confidence` MUST be a number in `[0, 1]`.\n459: 3. Each `evidenceRefs` entry MUST contain a `:` separating the path from a line or range.\n460: 4. `finalSeverity` MUST match the severity the finding is registered under in the iteration's `Findings` section and in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`.\n461: 5. When any rule fails, the workflow appends `{\"event\":\"claim_adjudication\",\"passed\":false,\"missingPackets\":[...]}` to the state log. The next `step_check_convergence` call reads that event and sets `claimAdjudicationGate` = `false`, producing a `blockedStop` event with `blockedBy: [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]` until a follow-up iteration rewrites the packet.\n462: \n463: ### Severity Transition Rules\n464: \n465: - **P2 → P1**: confirmed exploitable impact or spec violation with direct evidence\n466: - **P1 → P0**: demonstrated data loss, security breach, or hard-gate failure\n467: - **Downgrade**: requires explicit counterevidence or a confirmed alternative explanation\n468: - Every transition is recorded in the packet's `transitions` array and mirrored into the finding registry's `transitions` field\n469: \n470: ---\n471: \n472: ## 10. FINDING REGISTRY\n473: \n474: Each finding is tracked with a unique identifier enabling deduplication, severity transitions, and status lifecycle.\n475: \n476: ### Schema\n477: \n478: ```json\n479: {\n480:   \"findingId\": \"F003\",\n481:   \"severity\": \"P1\",\n482:   \"category\": \"resource-map-coverage\",\n483:   \"status\": \"active\",\n484:   \"dimension\": \"traceability\",\n485:   \"title\": \"Applied target file missing from resource-map inventory\",\n486:   \"file\": \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review.yaml\",\n487:   \"line\": 955,\n488:   \"firstSeen\": 2,\n489:   \"lastSeen\": 4,\n490:   \"transitions\": [\n491:     { \"iteration\": 2, \"from\": null, \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"Initial discovery\" },\n492:     { \"iteration\": 4, \"from\": \"P2\", \"to\": \"P1\", \"reason\": \"Confirmed real coverage gap against applied target inventory\" }\n493:   ]\n494: }\n495: ```\n496: \n497: | Field | Type | Description |\n498: |-------|------|-------------|\n499: | findingId | string | Sequential unique ID: `F001`, `F002`, ... |\n500: | severity | `\"P0\"` / `\"P1\"` / `\"P2\"` | Current severity |\n501: | category | `\"correctness\"` / `\"security\"` / `\"traceability\"` / `\"maintainability\"` / `\"resource-map-coverage\"` | Primary audit category for the finding, `resource-map-coverage` is reserved for implementation-vs-map coverage gaps |\n502: | status | `\"active\"` / `\"resolved\"` / `\"deferred\"` / `\"disproved\"` | Current status |\n503: | dimension | string | Primary dimension: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability |\n504: | title | string | Short description |\n505: | file | string | File path |\n506: | line | number | Line number (approximate) |\n507: | firstSeen / lastSeen | number | Iteration where first discovered / last referenced |\n508: | transitions | array | Severity and status change history |\n509: \n510: ### Status Lifecycle\n511: \n512: ```text\n513: [discovered] --> active --> resolved    (fixed or confirmed non-issue)\n514:                   |\n515:                   +--> deferred    (advisory, below threshold)\n516:                   |\n517:                   +--> disproved   (counterevidence invalidated)\n518: ```\n519: \n520: | Status | Counts Toward Verdict |\n521: |--------|----------------------|\n522: | active | Yes |\n523: | resolved | No |\n524: | deferred | No (listed in Deferred Items) |\n525: | disproved | No |\n526: \n527: ### Deduplication\n528: \n529: Same file + line range + root cause as an existing finding = **refinement**, not new. The existing findingId is updated. Refinements count at half weight (`refinementMultiplier: 0.5`) and are tracked via `findingsRefined` in JSONL.\n530: \n531: ### Cross-Reference Protocols\n532: \n533: | Protocol | Level | Applies To | Gate |\n534: |----------|-------|------------|------|\n535: | spec_code | core | all types | hard |\n536: | checklist_evidence | core | all types | hard |\n537: | skill_agent | overlay | skill | advisory |\n538: | agent_cross_runtime | overlay | agent | advisory |\n539: | feature_catalog_code | overlay | skill, spec-folder, track, files | advisory |\n540: | playbook_capability | overlay | skill, agent, spec-folder | advisory |\n541: \n542: Severity for `resource-map-coverage` findings is calibrated to the coverage-gate outcome:\n543: - `P2` when an untouched map entry is explicitly `expected-by-scope`\n544: - `P1` when an untouched or absent path represents a real coverage gap\n545: - `P0` only when the missing coverage masks a release-blocking correctness or security risk\n546: \n547: ### Quality Gates\n548: \n549: | Gate | Rule |\n550: |------|------|\n551: | Evidence | Every active finding backed by concrete file:line evidence |\n552: | Scope | Reviewed files and conclusions stay inside declared scope |\n553: | Coverage | Required dimensions and required protocols covered |\n554: \n555: All three gates must pass before STOP. Gate failure forces `verdict: \"FAIL\"` regardless of finding counts.\n556: \n557: ---\n558: \n559: ## 11. LEDGER VOCABULARY AND PROJECTION CEILING\n560: \n561: ### Registered vocabulary\n562: \n563: The canonical dotted stems for this mode live in `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-review-ledger-schema/deep-review-ledger-types.ts`:\n564: \n565: - `DeepReviewEventStems` — the registered stems the ledger accepts.\n566: - `DEEP_REVIEW_STEM_PRODUCERS` — one entry per stem recording whether a mechanical producer emits it today (`spoken`, with the producer files) or why nothing does (`reserved`).\n567: \n568: The registry is only honest while it matches the emitter surface. `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs` scans the workflow assets and runtime scripts and fails (exit 2) when a registered stem has no producer, a spoken stem has no emitter, or a reserved stem is emitted anyway:\n569: \n570: ```bash\n571: node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/check-ledger-stem-producers.cjs\n572: ```\n573: \n574: ### Which file is authoritative\n575: \n576: `deep-review-state.jsonl` is authoritative while the mode's authority record (`authority-deep-review.json`, state `legacy_authoritative`) names the legacy writer. Once the record moves to `new_authoritative_reversible` or `new_authoritative_final` with `selectedWriter: \"dark\"`, the ledger is authoritative and this file becomes a projection that the append gateway refreshes after each append.\n577: \n578: ### What a projection refresh can reproduce\n579: \n580: The projection folds only registered stems, and its `run_initialized` arm rebuilds a thin config row: `type`, `topic`, `maxIterations`, `generation`, `timestamp`. A pre-flip config row written by the workflow carries attribution the fold cannot rebuild — `mode`, `reviewTarget`, `reviewTargetType`, `reviewDimensions`, `resource_map_present`, `resource_map`, `sessionId`, `parentSessionId`, `lineageMode`, `continuedFromRun`, `convergenceThreshold`, `antiConvergence`, `stopPolicy`, `executor`, `createdAt`, `specFolder`.\n581: \n582: Because losing those keys silently would make the projection look complete while the operator's context is gone, a replace that would drop keys from an existing `type: \"config\"` first row is refused with `ATTRIBUTION_COLLAPSE` (invariant `no-attribution-loss-on-replace`) before any bytes are written. An operator who hits it either migrates the attribution into a registered `deep_review.run_initialized` payload or intentionally moves the legacy file aside to accept the loss."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/references/state/state-format.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760625335,"end":1794760626150}}}}
