/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:83:| `SYSTEM_TASK_DISPATCH_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables task-dispatch warnings and denials. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/`, `.opencode/plugins/system-deep-loop-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:84:| `SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables operator decision capture: the answer hooks and plugins queue nothing and the stop hook sends no save nudge. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/`, `.opencode/plugins/decision-capture.js`, `hooks/claude/session-stop.ts` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:85:| `SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the ask-surface guard: a turn ending in a typed option menu is neither sent back nor logged as a fire. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/ask-surface-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/ask-surface-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:86:| `SYSTEM_ENV_SECRET_GUARD_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the dotenv guard: reads and writes of `.env` files are no longer refused, the after-call check stops, and the three OpenCode inspection tools report that they are disabled. Read from the process environment only, never from `hook-flags.env`, which an agent can write. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/env-secret-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:87:| `SYSTEM_OVERLAY_GUARD_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Turns the whole overlay guard off: an edit to a file a vendored copy's overlay owns is no longer refused, and with `strictWrites` on neither is a write no overlay owns. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/overlay-guard.js` |\n=== hook flags table in hooks README ===\n42-| Concern | Canonical flag (`SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`) | Legacy aliases | Default | Effect | Status |\n43-|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n45-| `spec-gate` | `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | enabled | notice / deny | wired |\n46-| `completion` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n--\n78-Flags resolve from two places: the live environment, and an optional config file. The environment always wins, so a persisted default can still be overridden for one session.\n79-\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n82-\n83-```bash\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74:| `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Master switch for every concern below. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:78:| `CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Codex hook-drift warnings. No aliases. | `.opencode/plugins/codex-hooks-watchdog.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:79:| `SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Devin permission-policy decisions. No aliases. | `hooks/devin/permission-request-policy.mjs` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:80:| `SYSTEM_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables directive lifecycle boundary handling. No aliases. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts`, `hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:82:| `SK_CODE_POST_EDIT_QUALITY_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables post-edit quality warnings. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/post-edit-quality/`, `.opencode/plugins/sk-code-post-edit-quality.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:83:| `SYSTEM_TASK_DISPATCH_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables task-dispatch warnings and denials. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/task-dispatch/`, `.opencode/plugins/system-deep-loop-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:84:| `SYSTEM_DECISION_CAPTURE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables operator decision capture: the answer hooks and plugins queue nothing and the stop hook sends no save nudge. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/decision-capture/`, `.opencode/plugins/decision-capture.js`, `hooks/claude/session-stop.ts` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:85:| `SYSTEM_ASK_SURFACE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the ask-surface guard: a turn ending in a typed option menu is neither sent back nor logged as a fire. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/ask-surface-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/ask-surface-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:86:| `SYSTEM_ENV_SECRET_GUARD_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables the dotenv guard: reads and writes of `.env` files are no longer refused, the after-call check stops, and the three OpenCode inspection tools report that they are disabled. Read from the process environment only, never from `hook-flags.env`, which an agent can write. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/env-secret-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/env-secret-guard.js` |\n.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:87:| `SYSTEM_OVERLAY_GUARD_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Turns the whole overlay guard off: an edit to a file a vendored copy's overlay owns is no longer refused, and with `strictWrites` on neither is a write no overlay owns. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/overlay-guard/`, `.opencode/plugins/overlay-guard.js` |\n=== hook flags table in hooks README ===\n42-| Concern | Canonical flag (`SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED`) | Legacy aliases | Default | Effect | Status |\n43-|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n45-| `spec-gate` | `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | enabled | notice / deny | wired |\n46-| `completion` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | enabled | warn | wired |\n--\n78-Flags resolve from two places: the live environment, and an optional config file. The environment always wins, so a persisted default can still be overridden for one session.\n79-\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n82-\n83-```bash\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"No aliases\\\\|aliases\\\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md | head -10 && echo \\\"=== hook flags table in hooks README ===\\\" && grep -n -B2 -A2 \\\"SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760990690,"end":1794760991809}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794760991816,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0175cd2002F1mViCj3UbaSD9","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e0165e40001PCNQ065O9pACQO","type":"tool","id":"call_bcf2a835dbb94ee7bf786307","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"SKILL_ADVISOR\\|skill-advisor\" .skilled/hooks/README.md | head -20 && echo \"=== ENV ref 60-80 ===\" && sed -n 60,80p .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md"},"output":"44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n106:Hooks that did **not** move keep their code inside their owning skill because their core logic genuinely is that skill's engine, not a bolt-on guard: `spec-gate-*`, the session-lifecycle hooks, and `completion-evidence-stop` (`system-spec-kit`), the skill-advisor brief (`system-skill-advisor`), and `git-preflight-advisory` (`sk-git`, depends on its own `git-context.mjs`/`git-rule-checks.mjs` rule engine). Their code stays there, but each now has an index symlink under `<concern>/<runtime>/` here (see Full index above) and honors the `isHookEnabled` kill-switch.\n228:**Skill-owned concerns are indexed here too**: the tree above shows only the concerns whose *real code* lives in this hub. Every skill-owned concern is additionally present as per-runtime symlinks under `<concern>/<runtime>/` (real code stays in the owning skill, as \"Full index + kill-switches\" above describes): `skill-advisor/`, `spec-gate/`, `session-lifecycle/`, `completion/`, `directive-lifecycle/`, `git-preflight/`, `git-message-gate/`, `dist-freshness/`, `codex-watchdog/`, and `permission-policy/`. The same pattern covers the bin-backed concerns: `git-live-follow/` and `git-primary-reconcile/` hold one symlink per runtime into `.skilled/bin/` and are indexed in the additional-hooks table below. DSH's skill-owned adapters follow it too: `skill-advisor/dsh/`, `spec-gate/dsh/`, `session-lifecycle/dsh/`, `completion/dsh/`, `git-preflight/dsh/` and `git-message-gate/dsh/` hold index links to the real files in `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/`, `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/dsh/` and `sk-git/scripts/hooks/dsh/`. Vibe's guard scripts in skill-owned concerns are indexed the same way: `spec-gate/vibe/`, `dist-freshness/vibe/`, `git-message-gate/vibe/` and `session-cleanup/vibe/` hold links to `.vibe/plugins/repo-guards/`.\n289:node --test .skilled/hooks/*/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/ .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.test.mjs\n339:| `directive-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in `system-skill-advisor` lifecycle state | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.ts` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.mjs` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in the Vibe turn-start advisor part |\n351:| `session-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | by-design: session events run inside the concern plugins (`system-skill-advisor`, `opencode-goal`, `session-cleanup`) | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n353:| `skill-advisor` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n371:The `session-lifecycle/` and `skill-advisor/` subfolders of Claude, Codex, Cursor and Devin also carry the deployed `.js` entrypoint alongside its `.ts` source: a relative symlink into `system-spec-kit`'s built `dist/hooks/`, so the actually-executed file is browsable too. Those dist symlinks resolve after a build, exactly like the deployed `.<runtime>/hooks/*.js` symlinks the runtimes already use. Pi and DSH keep only their `.ts` or `.mjs` source in those folders, and `skill-advisor/opencode/` links the OpenCode plugin itself.\n=== ENV ref 60-80 ===\n- Headline multipliers stay blocked unless prompt, completion, cache-read, and cache-write token fields all have `provider_counted` authority. Later packets should reuse `canPublishMultiplier()` instead of inventing packet-local gates.\n- Publication-grade rows must carry methodology metadata with `schemaVersion`, `methodologyStatus`, and at least one provenance entry before they can be emitted.\n- No environment variable disables or downgrades this contract. The telemetry and eval toggles that once fed it were removed with the memory engine, and nothing replaced them.\n\n### Hook kill-switches\n\nEvery repo-authored hook concern is enabled by default except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. Its enable flags decide in order: the runtime's own `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one, and with both empty only Claude Code runs. Set the master flag or one canonical concern flag to a truthy value (`1`, `true`, `yes`, or `on`, case-insensitive) to disable that surface. Resolver failures are fail-open.\n\nFlags can be set as environment variables **or** in a config file: copy `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example` to `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (gitignored) and set the same `KEY=value` names there. A real environment variable always overrides the file, so a persisted default can be flipped back for one session. `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` overrides the config file path.\n\n**These names are derived, not written down.** `concernFlag()` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` builds the default shape `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` from the concern slug, and `CONCERN_CANONICAL` overrides it for the six concerns owned by a named surface (`goal`, `dispatch`, `mcp-route-guard`, `codex-watchdog`, `git-preflight`, `post-edit-quality`). Grepping the repo for one of the derived names therefore finds nothing, which is expected and not evidence the flag is dead. The Source column below names the surface the concern gates, not a literal read site.\n\n| Variable | Default | Type | Description | Source |\n|----------|---------|------|-------------|--------|\n| `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Master switch for every concern below. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}` |\n| `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables skill-advisor injection and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. Aliases: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | disable flag (1) | Disables Gate-3 delivery and enforcement. Alias: `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED`. | `hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`, `.opencode/plugins/system-spec-gate.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables completion-evidence warnings. Aliases: `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED`. | `hooks/*/completion-evidence*`, `.opencode/plugins/system-completion-sentinel.js` |\n| `CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Codex hook-drift warnings. No aliases. | `.opencode/plugins/codex-hooks-watchdog.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Devin permission-policy decisions. No aliases. | `hooks/devin/permission-request-policy.mjs` |\n| `SYSTEM_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables directive lifecycle boundary handling. No aliases. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts`, `hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"44:| `skill-advisor` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` | enabled | inject | wired |\n80:- **Environment**: set any flag inline (`SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1 <command>`), for a session (`export SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED=1`), or in your shell profile.\n81:- **Config file**: copy `hook-flags.env.example` to `hook-flags.env` (in this directory) and uncomment the flags you want off. It uses the same `KEY=value` names, is gitignored (personal to you), and is read by every guard variant. A comment can follow a value after a space or tab, so the example's lines work as soon as you uncomment them. Re-enable a file-disabled hook for one session with e.g. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=0`. `/doctor:env` shows where each switch is set and writes one here after your yes, and the root `.env.example` lists every other setting with its default.\n106:Hooks that did **not** move keep their code inside their owning skill because their core logic genuinely is that skill's engine, not a bolt-on guard: `spec-gate-*`, the session-lifecycle hooks, and `completion-evidence-stop` (`system-spec-kit`), the skill-advisor brief (`system-skill-advisor`), and `git-preflight-advisory` (`sk-git`, depends on its own `git-context.mjs`/`git-rule-checks.mjs` rule engine). Their code stays there, but each now has an index symlink under `<concern>/<runtime>/` here (see Full index above) and honors the `isHookEnabled` kill-switch.\n228:**Skill-owned concerns are indexed here too**: the tree above shows only the concerns whose *real code* lives in this hub. Every skill-owned concern is additionally present as per-runtime symlinks under `<concern>/<runtime>/` (real code stays in the owning skill, as \"Full index + kill-switches\" above describes): `skill-advisor/`, `spec-gate/`, `session-lifecycle/`, `completion/`, `directive-lifecycle/`, `git-preflight/`, `git-message-gate/`, `dist-freshness/`, `codex-watchdog/`, and `permission-policy/`. The same pattern covers the bin-backed concerns: `git-live-follow/` and `git-primary-reconcile/` hold one symlink per runtime into `.skilled/bin/` and are indexed in the additional-hooks table below. DSH's skill-owned adapters follow it too: `skill-advisor/dsh/`, `spec-gate/dsh/`, `session-lifecycle/dsh/`, `completion/dsh/`, `git-preflight/dsh/` and `git-message-gate/dsh/` hold index links to the real files in `system-skill-advisor/hooks/dsh/`, `system-spec-kit/runtime/hooks/dsh/` and `sk-git/scripts/hooks/dsh/`. Vibe's guard scripts in skill-owned concerns are indexed the same way: `spec-gate/vibe/`, `dist-freshness/vibe/`, `git-message-gate/vibe/` and `session-cleanup/vibe/` hold links to `.vibe/plugins/repo-guards/`.\n289:node --test .skilled/hooks/*/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/tests/dsh-*.test.mjs .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/tests/ .skilled/hooks/decision-capture/bin/sweep-dsh.test.mjs\n339:| `directive-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in the shared `user-prompt-submit` lifecycle | by-design: embedded in `system-skill-advisor` lifecycle state | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.ts` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in `prompt-advisor.mjs` directive de-dup | by-design: embedded in the Vibe turn-start advisor part |\n351:| `session-lifecycle` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | by-design: session events run inside the concern plugins (`system-skill-advisor`, `opencode-goal`, `session-cleanup`) | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n353:| `skill-advisor` | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered | ✓ covered |\n371:The `session-lifecycle/` and `skill-advisor/` subfolders of Claude, Codex, Cursor and Devin also carry the deployed `.js` entrypoint alongside its `.ts` source: a relative symlink into `system-spec-kit`'s built `dist/hooks/`, so the actually-executed file is browsable too. Those dist symlinks resolve after a build, exactly like the deployed `.<runtime>/hooks/*.js` symlinks the runtimes already use. Pi and DSH keep only their `.ts` or `.mjs` source in those folders, and `skill-advisor/opencode/` links the OpenCode plugin itself.\n=== ENV ref 60-80 ===\n- Headline multipliers stay blocked unless prompt, completion, cache-read, and cache-write token fields all have `provider_counted` authority. Later packets should reuse `canPublishMultiplier()` instead of inventing packet-local gates.\n- Publication-grade rows must carry methodology metadata with `schemaVersion`, `methodologyStatus`, and at least one provenance entry before they can be emitted.\n- No environment variable disables or downgrades this contract. The telemetry and eval toggles that once fed it were removed with the memory engine, and nothing replaced them.\n\n### Hook kill-switches\n\nEvery repo-authored hook concern is enabled by default except `session-handover`, which ships on for Claude Code and off for every other runtime. Its enable flags decide in order: the runtime's own `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_<RUNTIME>_ENABLED` when it holds a value, then `SYSTEM_SESSION_HANDOVER_ENABLED` when it holds one, and with both empty only Claude Code runs. Set the master flag or one canonical concern flag to a truthy value (`1`, `true`, `yes`, or `on`, case-insensitive) to disable that surface. Resolver failures are fail-open.\n\nFlags can be set as environment variables **or** in a config file: copy `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example` to `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env` (gitignored) and set the same `KEY=value` names there. A real environment variable always overrides the file, so a persisted default can be flipped back for one session. `HOOK_FLAGS_CONFIG` overrides the config file path.\n\n**These names are derived, not written down.** `concernFlag()` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs` builds the default shape `SYSTEM_<CONCERN>_DISABLED` from the concern slug, and `CONCERN_CANONICAL` overrides it for the six concerns owned by a named surface (`goal`, `dispatch`, `mcp-route-guard`, `codex-watchdog`, `git-preflight`, `post-edit-quality`). Grepping the repo for one of the derived names therefore finds nothing, which is expected and not evidence the flag is dead. The Source column below names the surface the concern gates, not a literal read site.\n\n| Variable | Default | Type | Description | Source |\n|----------|---------|------|-------------|--------|\n| `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Master switch for every concern below. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}` |\n| `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables skill-advisor injection and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. Aliases: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | disable flag (1) | Disables Gate-3 delivery and enforcement. Alias: `SPECKIT_SPEC_GATE_DISABLED`. | `hooks/lib/spec-gate/spec-gate-core.mjs`, `.opencode/plugins/system-spec-gate.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables completion-evidence warnings. Aliases: `SYSTEM_COMPLETION_SENTINEL_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SPECKIT_COMPLETION_DISABLED`. | `hooks/*/completion-evidence*`, `.opencode/plugins/system-completion-sentinel.js` |\n| `CODEX_WATCHDOG_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Codex hook-drift warnings. No aliases. | `.opencode/plugins/codex-hooks-watchdog.js` |\n| `SYSTEM_PERMISSION_POLICY_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables Devin permission-policy decisions. No aliases. | `hooks/devin/permission-request-policy.mjs` |\n| `SYSTEM_DIRECTIVE_LIFECYCLE_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables directive lifecycle boundary handling. No aliases. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts`, `hooks/claude/directive-lifecycle-boundary.ts` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"SKILL_ADVISOR\\\\|skill-advisor\\\" .skilled/hooks/README.md | head -20 && echo \\\"=== ENV ref 60-80 ===\\\" && sed -n 60,80p .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794760989906,"end":1794760991816}}}}
