{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761109510,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0192c5a001WigTExCZvruBc5","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e0190496001ZfffnHDN77Pxrp","type":"tool","id":"call_2b1022d4c4384e3cb6171c8f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && head -60 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md && echo \"=== strategy anchors ===\" && sed -n 1,80p specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — accuracy-runner-4 (pass four)\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=accuracy-runner-4; sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict:** CONDITIONAL\n- **hasAdvisories:** false (the verdict is CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are still advisories)\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 2, P2 = 7\n- **Review scope:** the pass-four `accuracy-runner` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`: the routing-accuracy capture and committed baseline, the transcript scorer and its summary, the command-offer attribution module, the three vitest files that pin them, and the shared README that describes them. Six code/test files changed since pass three plus the README and the baseline.\n- **Operator review focus:** Code review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4.txt: it names the scope file, which files your lineage reviews, the checks and the severity rules. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n- **Headline:** the pass-four offer fix is dead before it reaches a run line: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute `offeredAs`, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner-side branch reads it. The new fit/decline tally records that 8 of 24 refusal/question/small-edit/app-problem rows still carry a command, but the rows never reach the `false_offer` gate and the count is only checked against itself. The remaining seven findings are a heredoc delimiter gap, a start/loop gap for shell reads, a live holdout guard that reads the baseline, an unpinned stage/fit ratchet, a `--pair` doc mismatch, a `paired` arm key collision and a dead `unscoredOnly` field.\n- **Loop state:** `maxIterations=4` reached; the coverage graph was unavailable, so a legal graph-backed STOP was not claimable. Release readiness is `in-progress`, not `converged`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **required** for this lineage: two active P1 findings remain and both are in the pass-four change surface. The seven P2s are advisories for the remediation owner.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": 9,\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": 3,\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Pin the run-line offer schema: offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, offeredAs and offerError are one record, and every producer writes all four\",\n    \"State the fit-gate contract: which row kinds must stay command-free, which mutating commands are forbidden, and whether carried > baseline fails the ratchet\",\n    \"State the holdout publication rule for the live capture, not only the committed baseline\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add offeredAs to backfillRunLog and run-command-behaviour appendRunLine, and a backfill test whose replay returns partner\",\n    \"Include the fit/decline rows in a gate or add a baseline comparison plus a threshold; decide the accepted 8 of 24\",\n    \"Add a live holdout publication assertion and baseline comparisons for plain_stages and fit.carried\",\n    \"Broaden the heredoc delimiter grammar and wire shell reads into startState/takenLoop\",\n    \"Reserve the paired arm key and remove or wire workflow.unscoredOnly\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\n    \"correctness/cross-consumer\",\n    \"security/measurement-gate\",\n    \"correctness/measurement\",\n    \"security/evaluation-integrity\",\n    \"traceability/ratchet\",\n    \"traceability/documentation\",\n    \"maintainability/reserved-key\",\n    \"maintainability/dead-field\"\n  ],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n=== strategy anchors ===\n# Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-4 Lineage\n\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n- Fan-out lineage: `accuracy-runner-4` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4`); pass-four area is `accuracy-runner`\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=4`, whichever comes first\n- Success criteria: every pass-four area file reviewed; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete input; holdout hygiene verified by counts only; docs that disagree with code reported\n- Review focus (operator bound): pass-four code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-4.txt` first. Review the files whose area is `accuracy-runner` plus shared docs that describe them: the routing-accuracy capture, the transcript scorer, the offer attribution module and their tests. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; whether a refusal, a question or a mention can still attach or start a mutating command; whether the transcript scorer counts a load, a followed step or an offer that did not happen (Codex exec bodies, rg and grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges); holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code.\n- Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nCommand surfacing behaviour for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the pass-four `accuracy-runner` area: the routing-accuracy capture and its committed baseline, the transcript scorer and its run-log summary, the command-offer attribution module, and the three vitest files that pin them.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n[All dimensions complete]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin` or `doctor-docs` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n- Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n- Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n- Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n- `maxIterations=4` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n- Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n- [x] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 2\n- P2 (Suggestions): 7\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the slice file's baseline comparisons with the new attached-metrics blocks found that the stage and fit counts are invariant-tested but never baseline-pinned (iteration 3).\n- Treating the summary as one key space found that `unscored` is reserved but `paired` is not, and that `workflow.unscoredOnly` is never written (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — accuracy-runner-4 (pass four)\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=accuracy-runner-4; sessionId=fanout-accuracy-runner-4-1794669272137-9v23rz; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict:** CONDITIONAL\n- **hasAdvisories:** false (the verdict is CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are still advisories)\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 2, P2 = 7\n- **Review scope:** the pass-four `accuracy-runner` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`: the routing-accuracy capture and committed baseline, the transcript scorer and its summary, the command-offer attribution module, the three vitest files that pin them, and the shared README that describes them. Six code/test files changed since pass three plus the README and the baseline.\n- **Operator review focus:** Code review pass four of command surfacing. FIRST read and follow specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-brief-4.txt: it names the scope file, which files your lineage reviews, the checks and the severity rules. HOLDOUT RULE: never open command-prompts.jsonl or holdout-prompts.jsonl except through jq 'del(.prompt)', never run git diff, show or log -p over a path that includes command-prompts.jsonl without the pathspec ':(exclude)**/command-prompts.jsonl', and never print a prompt whose split is holdout. The reviewer changes no code and writes only inside its lineage folder.\n- **Headline:** the pass-four offer fix is dead before it reaches a run line: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute `offeredAs`, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner-side branch reads it. The new fit/decline tally records that 8 of 24 refusal/question/small-edit/app-problem rows still carry a command, but the rows never reach the `false_offer` gate and the count is only checked against itself. The remaining seven findings are a heredoc delimiter gap, a start/loop gap for shell reads, a live holdout guard that reads the baseline, an unpinned stage/fit ratchet, a `--pair` doc mismatch, a `paired` arm key collision and a dead `unscoredOnly` field.\n- **Loop state:** `maxIterations=4` reached; the coverage graph was unavailable, so a legal graph-backed STOP was not claimable. Release readiness is `in-progress`, not `converged`.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\n`/speckit:plan` is **required** for this lineage: two active P1 findings remain and both are in the pass-four change surface. The seven P2s are advisories for the remediation owner.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"activeFindings\": 9,\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": 3,\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"Pin the run-line offer schema: offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, offeredAs and offerError are one record, and every producer writes all four\",\n    \"State the fit-gate contract: which row kinds must stay command-free, which mutating commands are forbidden, and whether carried > baseline fails the ratchet\",\n    \"State the holdout publication rule for the live capture, not only the committed baseline\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Add offeredAs to backfillRunLog and run-command-behaviour appendRunLine, and a backfill test whose replay returns partner\",\n    \"Include the fit/decline rows in a gate or add a baseline comparison plus a threshold; decide the accepted 8 of 24\",\n    \"Add a live holdout publication assertion and baseline comparisons for plain_stages and fit.carried\",\n    \"Broaden the heredoc delimiter grammar and wire shell reads into startState/takenLoop\",\n    \"Reserve the paired arm key and remove or wire workflow.unscoredOnly\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\n    \"correctness/cross-consumer\",\n    \"security/measurement-gate\",\n    \"correctness/measurement\",\n    \"security/evaluation-integrity\",\n    \"traceability/ratchet\",\n    \"traceability/documentation\",\n    \"maintainability/reserved-key\",\n    \"maintainability/dead-field\"\n  ],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs\",\n    \"runtime/tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts\",\n    \"runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n=== strategy anchors ===\n# Deep Review Strategy - accuracy-runner-4 Lineage\n\n## 1. REVIEW CHARTER\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder target)\n- Fan-out lineage: `accuracy-runner-4` (artifact dir `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4`); pass-four area is `accuracy-runner`\n- Dimensions: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability\n- Stop conditions: legal convergence at `convergenceThreshold=0.10`, or `maxIterations=4`, whichever comes first\n- Success criteria: every pass-four area file reviewed; every finding carries `file:line` and a concrete input; holdout hygiene verified by counts only; docs that disagree with code reported\n- Review focus (operator bound): pass-four code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-4.txt` first. Review the files whose area is `accuracy-runner` plus shared docs that describe them: the routing-accuracy capture, the transcript scorer, the offer attribution module and their tests. Check behaviour on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh; whether a refusal, a question or a mention can still attach or start a mutating command; whether the transcript scorer counts a load, a followed step or an offer that did not happen (Codex exec bodies, rg and grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges); holdout hygiene; docs that disagree with code.\n- Resource map: `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nCommand surfacing behaviour for the routed skill/command advisor, restricted to the pass-four `accuracy-runner` area: the routing-accuracy capture and its committed baseline, the transcript scorer and its run-log summary, the command-offer attribution module, and the three vitest files that pin them.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n[All dimensions complete]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Not reviewing `scorer-attach`, `render-hooks-plugin` or `doctor-docs` area files except as read-only context when a cross-area contract is required\n- Not fixing anything: the review is observation-only\n- Not reading or printing holdout prompt text; holdout coverage is counts-only\n- Not running repo tooling that writes outside the lineage; runners are audited by reading\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Legal convergence (all dimensions covered plus stabilization) at or below `convergenceThreshold`\n- `maxIterations=4` reached (`stopReason: maxIterationsReached`)\n- Any active P0 blocks a PASS verdict but does not stop iteration dispatch by itself; the P0 override keeps `newFindingsRatio >= 0.50`\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n- [x] security\n- [x] traceability\n- [x] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 2\n- P2 (Suggestions): 7\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the producer and its consumer together found the dead `offeredAs` field: `parseOffer`/`replayOffer` compute it, both writers drop it, and the scorer's partner branch reads it (iteration 1).\n- Checking the heredoc filter against a delimiter outside its grammar found a body line that the new shell reader parses as a read (iteration 1).\n- Asking which detector consumes the new shell-read capability found that `readDocument`/`takenLoop` do not, so a Codex shell read is a load but not a start or a loop (iteration 1).\n- Reading the new fit branch against the silence tally found that the 24 decline rows are removed before `false_offer`, so the baseline's 8 carried commands cannot fail anything (iteration 2).\n- Asking whether the holdout publication test reads the live capture or the committed file found that it reads only the baseline, and the live row comparison filters holdout ids out (iteration 2).\n- Comparing the slice file's baseline comparisons with the new attached-metrics blocks found that the stage and fit counts are invariant-tested but never baseline-pinned (iteration 3).\n- Treating the summary as one key space found that `unscored` is reserved but `paired` is not, and that `workflow.unscoredOnly` is never written (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking the offer field only in the parser and the scorer looked clean; only `rg` over every writer showed that no run line ever carries the new field (iteration 1).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && head -60 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/review-report.md && echo \\\"=== strategy anchors ===\\\" && sed -n 1,80p specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761108570,"end":1794761109510}}}}
