{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761194613,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01a75a80022NzJcJAUra0p9P","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e01a5585001MpfAEMAeGRG3Mr","type":"tool","id":"call_86bc62531ece4dc49ee036a2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\\|SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1'\\|SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1'\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts && echo \"=== ENV ref rows ===\" && grep -n \"SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\|SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md && echo \"=== lib README lines 97-140 ===\" && sed -n 97,140p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md | cat -n"},"output":"124:  it('keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env', () => {\n130:      SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1',\n131:      SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1',\n=== ENV ref rows ===\n74:| `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Master switch for every concern below. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}` |\n75:| `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables skill-advisor injection and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. Aliases: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` |\n601:export SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1\n602:export SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1\n=== lib README lines 97-140 ===\n     1\t## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n     2\t\n     3\t```text\n     4\tlib/\n     5\t+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n     6\t+-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n     7\t+-- command-attach.ts\n     8\t+-- error-diagnostics.ts\n     9\t+-- freshness.ts\n    10\t+-- generation.ts\n    11\t+-- metrics.ts\n    12\t+-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n    13\t+-- policy-plan.ts\n    14\t+-- prompt-cache.ts\n    15\t+-- prompt-policy.ts\n    16\t+-- render.ts\n    17\t+-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n    18\t+-- source-cache.ts\n    19\t+-- subprocess.ts\n    20\t+-- cross-skill-edges/\n    21\t+-- embedders/\n    22\t+-- ipc/\n    23\t+-- scorer/\n    24\t+-- shared/\n    25\t`-- README.md\n    26\t```\n    27\t\n    28\t---\n    29\t\n    30\t## 5. KEY FILES\n    31\t\n    32\t| File | Responsibility |\n    33\t|---|---|\n    34\t| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n    35\t| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n    36\t| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n    37\t| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n    38\t| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n    39\t| `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n    40\t| `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n    41\t| `subprocess.ts` | Wraps external process execution for advisor scripts or probes. |\n    42\t| `df-idf.ts` | Computes DF/IDF statistics over the active corpus, excluding archived and future skills through `lifecycle/archive-handling`, with a cached variant and a debounced updater. Only tests and the stress suite import it today. |\n    43\t| `route-exclusions.ts` | Loads the operator denylist of skill ids the advisor never routes: `config/route-exclusions.json`, fully replaced by a gitignored `route-exclusions.local.json` when present, or the directory in `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR`. A missing or malformed file yields an empty set and never throws. |\n    44\t| `caller-context.ts` | Holds the per-request caller context (session id, transport, caller pid, `trusted` flag) in `AsyncLocalStorage`, read by the trusted-caller gate. |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"124:  it('keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env', () => {\n130:      SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1',\n131:      SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1',\n=== ENV ref rows ===\n74:| `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Master switch for every concern below. No aliases. | `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.{cjs,mjs,ts,sh}` |\n75:| `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED` | unset (enabled) | truthy disable flag | Disables skill-advisor injection and makes the `advisor_recommend` direct call abstain. Aliases: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`. | `system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js` |\n601:export SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1\n602:export SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1\n=== lib README lines 97-140 ===\n     1\t## 4. DIRECTORY TREE\n     2\t\n     3\t```text\n     4\tlib/\n     5\t+-- advisor-runtime-values.ts\n     6\t+-- affordance-normalizer.ts\n     7\t+-- command-attach.ts\n     8\t+-- error-diagnostics.ts\n     9\t+-- freshness.ts\n    10\t+-- generation.ts\n    11\t+-- metrics.ts\n    12\t+-- normalize-adapter-output.ts\n    13\t+-- policy-plan.ts\n    14\t+-- prompt-cache.ts\n    15\t+-- prompt-policy.ts\n    16\t+-- render.ts\n    17\t+-- skill-advisor-brief.ts\n    18\t+-- source-cache.ts\n    19\t+-- subprocess.ts\n    20\t+-- cross-skill-edges/\n    21\t+-- embedders/\n    22\t+-- ipc/\n    23\t+-- scorer/\n    24\t+-- shared/\n    25\t`-- README.md\n    26\t```\n    27\t\n    28\t---\n    29\t\n    30\t## 5. KEY FILES\n    31\t\n    32\t| File | Responsibility |\n    33\t|---|---|\n    34\t| `advisor-runtime-values.ts` | Runtime constants and defaults used by advisor paths. |\n    35\t| `affordance-normalizer.ts` | Normalizes prompt affordance signals before scoring. |\n    36\t| `command-attach.ts` | `attachCommand()` names the slash command for a hub recommendation whose compiled route picks one `workflowMode`. It reads the `MODE_COMMANDS` table that `derive-command-bridges.cjs` generates from each hub's `mode-registry.json`. A `system-deep-loop` command needs the same command typed in the prompt or a `DEPTH_WORDING` phrase, and a prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command. `commandOnlyMentioned()` reads how the prompt names a command, and a command the prompt refuses or asks about is not offered unless a later clause asks for it. A correction inside an existing document carries no `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` or `/create:manual-testing-playbook`. The module has no imports. |\n    37\t| `prompt-policy.ts` | Applies prompt-safe routing and rendering policy. |\n    38\t| `render.ts` | Renders advisor results into prompt-safe output. |\n    39\t| `skill-advisor-brief.ts` | Builds concise advisor recommendation briefs. |\n    40\t| `normalize-adapter-output.ts` | Normalizes adapter result shapes. |\n    41\t| `subprocess.ts` | Wraps external process execution for advisor scripts or probes. |\n    42\t| `df-idf.ts` | Computes DF/IDF statistics over the active corpus, excluding archived and future skills through `lifecycle/archive-handling`, with a cached variant and a debounced updater. Only tests and the stress suite import it today. |\n    43\t| `route-exclusions.ts` | Loads the operator denylist of skill ids the advisor never routes: `config/route-exclusions.json`, fully replaced by a gitignored `route-exclusions.local.json` when present, or the directory in `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_ROUTE_EXCLUSIONS_DIR`. A missing or malformed file yields an empty set and never throws. |\n    44\t| `caller-context.ts` | Holds the per-request caller context (session id, transport, caller pid, `trusted` flag) in `AsyncLocalStorage`, read by the trusted-caller gate. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\\\\|SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1'\\\\|SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED: '1'\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts && echo \\\"=== ENV ref rows ===\\\" && grep -n \\\"SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED\\\\|SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED\\\" .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md && echo \\\"=== lib README lines 97-140 ===\\\" && sed -n 97,140p .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md | cat -n\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761192872,"end":1794761194613}}}}
