emas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-169-  } catch {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-170-    return null;\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-171-  }\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-172-}\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-173-\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-174-/**\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-175- * True when the input, or a directory above it, holds a source-root entry\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-176- * (`.skilled` or `.opencode`) whose realpath is the source tree's own entry.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-177- *\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-178- * A project linked to a shared checkout holds `.skilled -> <source>/.skilled`\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-179- * while the daemon runs from the source tree, so the prefix allowlist alone\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-180- * refuses every linked project. Matching realpaths admits only a workspace that\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-181- * is actually wired to this source; a copied tree or a link to another source\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-182- * resolves elsewhere and stays refused.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-183- */\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-184-export function isWiredToSourceTree(input: string, sourceRoot: string = SOURCE_REPO_ROOT): boolean {\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts-1