{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761453576,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01e63cb001vBIjHxtVporfPf","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e01e4c19001v2IKlZbnKMsGlq","type":"tool","id":"call_5d794c482f3d46b085a4a220","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -66,14 +66,17 @@\n \n ---\n \n ## 6. WHAT WORKED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n+- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":5,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\",\"oldString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\",\"newString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761450443,"end":1794761453576}}}}
