{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761473484,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e01eb96f002qI5wzKx52eXNk6","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e01ea9cb001k4lTK6zjxFX4wi","type":"tool","id":"call_c30b0d4a0bf04acb99681c61","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && tail -20 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/iterations/iteration-001.md && echo \"=== strategy next-focus ===\" && sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/accuracy-runner-4/deep-review-strategy.md | head -20"},"output":"- `cd` in the same command resolves a bare document name against that folder, including a quoted folder with a trailing slash.\n- `offerOf` excludes a partner-side command when the line actually carries `offeredAs: 'partner'`; the unit test pins that branch.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A Codex body string that is not a command but names a document.** The every-string fallback only runs when no `cmd:` literal exists, and the test's list form is the intended shape; no real body in the area names a workflow document from a non-command string. Deferred as a hardening note, not a finding.\n- **`rg`/`grep` counted as a load.** Removed from `SHELL_READERS`; the shell reader also ignores a search's printed path.\n- **A `cd` that changes the folder for later commands.** The folder is carried across `&&`/`;` parts; the tests cover the quoted trailing-slash form.\n- **A read after the first write still counted as followed.** `followedBeforeWrite` compares the event position to the boundary; the existing negative tests hold.\n- **A `COMMAND:` line naming another command.** `offerSeenIn` filters through `namesCommand`; the declined-other-command test holds.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: the capture's fit/decline rows and the live holdout guard\n- Reason: the fit tally is the new measurement for refusals and questions, and the brief asks whether those rows can still carry or start a mutating command; the holdout guard must be checked against the live capture, not only the committed baseline\n- Rotation status: correctness complete; security next\n- Required evidence: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:560-700`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-267`, `command-routing-baseline.json:1961-1984`\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n=== strategy next-focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: none (maintainability is the last configured dimension) - Focus area: terminal synthesis and the active-finding replay - Reason: the loop reaches `maxIterations=4` after this iteration; the next step is the synthesis report and the closeout event, not another dispatch. The two active P1s keep the verdict CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are advisories. - Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains - Required evidence: the findings registry, all four iteration files and deltas, and the reducer's final state - Recovery note: the run did not reach a legal graph-backed convergence; the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`, and the report must say so. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"- `cd` in the same command resolves a bare document name against that folder, including a quoted folder with a trailing slash.\n- `offerOf` excludes a partner-side command when the line actually carries `offeredAs: 'partner'`; the unit test pins that branch.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A Codex body string that is not a command but names a document.** The every-string fallback only runs when no `cmd:` literal exists, and the test's list form is the intended shape; no real body in the area names a workflow document from a non-command string. Deferred as a hardening note, not a finding.\n- **`rg`/`grep` counted as a load.** Removed from `SHELL_READERS`; the shell reader also ignores a search's printed path.\n- **A `cd` that changes the folder for later commands.** The folder is carried across `&&`/`;` parts; the tests cover the quoted trailing-slash form.\n- **A read after the first write still counted as followed.** `followedBeforeWrite` compares the event position to the boundary; the existing negative tests hold.\n- **A `COMMAND:` line naming another command.** `offerSeenIn` filters through `namesCommand`; the declined-other-command test holds.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: security\n- Focus area: the capture's fit/decline rows and the live holdout guard\n- Reason: the fit tally is the new measurement for refusals and questions, and the brief asks whether those rows can still carry or start a mutating command; the holdout guard must be checked against the live capture, not only the committed baseline\n- Rotation status: correctness complete; security next\n- Required evidence: `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:560-700`, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:149-267`, `command-routing-baseline.json:1961-1984`\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n=== strategy next-focus ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: none (maintainability is the last configured dimension) - Focus area: terminal synthesis and the active-finding replay - Reason: the loop reaches `maxIterations=4` after this iteration; the next step is the synthesis report and the closeout event, not another dispatch. The two active P1s keep the verdict CONDITIONAL; the seven P2s are advisories. - Rotation status: all four dimensions covered; no new dimension remains - Required evidence: the findings registry, all four iteration files and deltas, and the reducer's final state - Recovery note: the run did not reach a legal graph-backed convergenc