{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794761607668,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"id":"prt_1e020c9f4001qyp70wzjlV57pp","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e020bcdf0019hnSZY5HmcuvUu","type":"step-start","snapshot":"61ba4da581e50173edc85896300c6b2e592e6e1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761613081,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e020cba400282Iv86yarR9BGj","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e020bcdf0019hnSZY5HmcuvUu","type":"tool","id":"call_25da9f781a0041e983a6b833","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).","oldString":"## 6. WHAT WORKED\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -69,13 +69,16 @@\n - Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\n - Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\n - Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n - Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n+- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n+- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n - Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\\n- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\",\"oldString\":\"## 6. WHAT WORKED\\n- Reading the resolver and both call sites together confirmed the switch decision precedes every daemon and scorer path; the no-daemon test pins the CLI half (iteration 1).\\n- Probing the built CLI read-only under four switch names (canonical, master, SPECKIT_ alias, MK_ alias) confirmed the envelope and the abstain reason without starting a daemon (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761608100,"end":1794761613081}}}}
