{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761721055,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0227343002RXuGEFhTJCH5pa","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e02266ad001QDUl0Gn6KZh0xE","type":"tool","id":"call_1d5020893132467ebebd834d","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n- Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n- Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n- Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).","oldString":"- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -71,14 +71,17 @@\n - Reading the CLI JSON manifest after the candidate workspace-root bypass showed `advisor_recommend` does not admit `workspaceRoot` at all, so the bypass has no reach and was ruled out (iteration 1).\n - Reading the launcher child-env filter against the pass-five diff confirmed the two switch names were removed from the exact-set allowlist (iteration 1).\n - Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n - Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n+- Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n+- Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n - Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n - Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n+- Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\\n- Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\\n- Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\\n- Trusting the launcher test's name (\\\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\\\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).\",\"oldString\":\"- Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\\n- Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761716547,"end":1794761721055}}}}
