{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761835594,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02431a2002B3yZ8UInv5q593","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e02426f0001HZ24QyxBb5Fp5r","type":"tool","id":"call_a54c9d8dc6144c41bcf0bc2a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n- Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n- Replaying the six active sites instead of opening a new direction confirmed the set is stable and that no P2 was silently downgraded in synthesis (iteration 4).\n- Reading the holdout files through `jq del(.prompt)` for counts only kept the hygiene rule while proving the files are present (224/63/36 rows) (iteration 4).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n- Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).\n- No clean route to a graph-backed convergence existed: the coverage graph stayed unavailable, so the run must stop at `maxIterationsReached` rather than claim `converged` (iteration 4).","oldString":"- Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n- Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n\n---\n\n## 7. WHAT FAILED\n- Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n- Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n- Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -74,15 +74,18 @@\n - Comparing the resolver's `MASTER_ALIASES` and `LEGACY_ALIASES` against the env index and the hooks README found the alias-column drift in one place instead of two guessed ones (iteration 2).\n - Reading CP-003's control command against the full alias set found a scenario defect that a switch-only read would miss; the read-only probe reproduced it under `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` (iteration 2).\n - Reading each test fixture against `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` rather than the test name found both boundary gaps: the launcher fixture sets two names and the CLI loop excludes the `MK_` set (iteration 3).\n - Listing `runtime/lib/*.ts` against the README tree found five missing modules and a second disagreement with the key-files table (iteration 3).\n+- Replaying the six active sites instead of opening a new direction confirmed the set is stable and that no P2 was silently downgraded in synthesis (iteration 4).\n+- Reading the holdout files through `jq del(.prompt)` for counts only kept the hygiene rule while proving the files are present (224/63/36 rows) (iteration 4).\n \n ---\n \n ## 7. WHAT FAILED\n - Checking `disabledRecommendOutput` alone made the workspace-root bypass look live; the CLI schema and the handler parse boundaries were needed to disprove it (iteration 1).\n - Reading the ENV-REFERENCE preamble as a licence to ignore the Source column was too generous: the row's own description claims the direct call, so the direct-call surface still has to be named (iteration 2).\n - Trusting the launcher test's name (\"keeps the per-request advisor switch out of the daemon env\") instead of its fixture would have marked the whole switch set covered; the fixture names only two keys (iteration 3).\n+- No clean route to a graph-backed convergence existed: the coverage graph stayed unavailable, so the run must stop at `maxIterationsReached` rather than claim `converged` (iteration 4).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"t