{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794761895339,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e02493ea001l3uQ6X7ThhF7Jn","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e0246b62001Pt8FPE0S5dNEh7","type":"tool","id":"call_8731c3ccbc344f95b71c29ec","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — kill-switch-cli-5 (pass five)\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=kill-switch-cli-5; sessionId=fanout-kill-switch-cli-5-1794760565927-i99t40; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Overall verdict:** PASS\n- **hasAdvisories:** true (six active P2 findings; no P0 or P1)\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 6\n- **Review scope:** the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. The reviewed files are `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example`, the CP-003 manual scenario, `runtime/lib/README.md`, the four switch test files, the shared CLI test utils and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md`, plus the shared docs that describe them (`INSTALL-GUIDE.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md`).\n- **Operator review focus:** pass-five code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-5.txt` first. Review the `kill-switch-cli` files plus docs that describe them. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal/question/history/mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open the three prompt files except through `jq del(.prompt)`; counts only. Change no code and write only inside the lineage folder.\n- **Headline:** the kill switch and the direct-call switch work on every path this area claims. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, its aliases, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` and a flags-file entry all make the CLI abstain before any daemon starts or the scorer runs; the daemon handler abstains from its own environment; the launcher's exact-set child-env allowlist no longer carries a switch, so a flagged caller cannot silence later callers. The six active P2s are documentation and test-maintenance gaps: the env index's alias column contradicts the resolver, the advisor row's Source column omits the direct-call readers, CP-003's control command does not isolate the full alias set, the launcher switch fixture covers two of ten names, the CLI alias loop excludes every `MK_` name, and the lib module map omits five modules.\n- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `converged` for this area: no active P0 or P1 remains, and the six P2s are advisories.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nNo remediation plan is required for this lineage: it has no active P0 or P1. The six P2s are advisories for a follow-up changelog/docs-maintenance pass.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"triggered\": false,\n  \"verdict\": \"PASS\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": true,\n  \"activeFindings\": 6,\n  \"nextCommand\": \"/create:changelog\",\n  \"remediationWorkstreams\": 2,\n  \"specSeed\": [\n    \"State the switch set as one table: canonical, aliases, master and the readers at the CLI, handler and prompt surfaces\",\n    \"State the CP-003 isolation rule: the control call must unset every name the resolver honors, not only the four in the scenario\"\n  ],\n  \"planSeed\": [\n    \"Fix ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75 and .skilled/hooks/README.md:44 to name the MK_ aliases and the direct-call readers\",\n    \"Extend the CP-003 control command to unset SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED and the MK_ names\",\n    \"Drive the launcher fixture from ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS instead of two literals\",\n    \"Assert abstention for the three MK_ names in the CLI disable loop without asserting the exact reason string\",\n    \"Refresh the runtime/lib/README.md directory tree against the real directory\"\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\n    \"traceability/alias-table\",\n    \"traceability/source-column\",\n    \"traceability/scenario-isolation\",\n    \"maintainability/test-fixture\",\n    \"maintainability/test-filter\",\n    \"maintainability/module-map\"\n  ],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md\",\n    \".skilled/hooks/README.md\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts\",\n    \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": false\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | Evidence | First / last seen | Status |\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|----------|-------------------|--------|\n| `iter2-P2-env-alias-column` | P2 | traceability | The master-switch row says \"No aliases\" while the resolver honors `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,256-258`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:20-33` | 2 / 4 | active |\n| `iter2-P2-env-source-column` | P2 | traceability | The advisor switch row's Source column omits the direct-call readers it claims | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:75`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:70-93`; `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1540`; `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:646` | 2 / 4 | active |\n| `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | P2 | traceability | CP-003's unflagged control call can abstain under a switch alias it never unsets | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49,80`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:41,70-78` | 2 / 4 | active |\n| `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` | P2 | maintainability | The launcher test covers two of the ten switch names it claims to keep out of the daemon env | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:124-145`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81` | 3 / 4 | active |\n| `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` | P2 | maintainability | The CLI disable loop filters out every `MK_` alias, so the direct-call path never exercises those names | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:219-221`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:20-49` | 3 / 4 | active |\n| `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | P2 | maintainability | The lib README tree omits five flat modules that exist on disk | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:100-122,138-140` | 3 / 4 | active |\n\nEvery active finding carries a concrete input in its iteration narrative; none relies on inference alone. The resolver and the CLI/handler/launcher switch paths are clean.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n| Lane | Findings | Order | Work |\n|------|----------|-------|------|\n| A. Switch docs and scenario | `iter2-P2-env-alias-column`, `iter2-P2-env-source-column`, `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | 1 | Correct the env index's alias and Source columns against `MASTER_ALIASES`/`LEGACY_ALIASES`, add the MK_ names, name the CLI/handler readers, and unset the full alias set in CP-003's control command. |\n| B. Switch tests and module map | `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture`, `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter`, `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | 2 | Drive the launcher fixture from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`, stop excluding `MK_` from the CLI abstain loop, and refresh the lib tree from the directory. |\n\nLane A does not depend on Lane B; both are advisory and can land in one documentation-maintenance change.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- Record the switch set as one canonical table: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, its aliases (including the `MK_` names), `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`, and the readers (`runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, the CLI, the daemon handler, the prompt hook and the plugin).\n- Record the disabled-envelope contract: empty recommendations, `freshness: unavailable`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED`, the deciding switch name, no prompt text, and the caller's workspace root.\n- Record the launcher isolation rule: the daemon child env is an exact-set allowlist and never carries a switch name.\n- Record the CP-003 control rule: the unflagged control call must unset every name the resolver honors, not only the four names in the current command.\n- Add a `## Rule overrides`-free, plain note that the lib README tree is a file map and must list every flat module.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n1. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44`: replace \"No aliases\" with the `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` alias; add the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names; add `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` and `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` to the advisor row's Source column.\n2. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49`: extend the `env -u` list with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` and `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`.\n3. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:127-145`: build the source env from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` so all ten names are filtered, keeping the exact-set assertion.\n4. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:221`: include the three `MK_` names and assert `recommendations: []` and `daemon.calls.length === 0` for them; assert the exact reason only for the names whose string is stable.\n5. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:100-122`: add `caller-context.ts`, `compiled-routing-flag.ts`, `df-idf.ts`, `private-skill-target.ts` and `route-exclusions.ts`, and align the key-files table with the tree.\n\nNo source change is required for the switch behavior itself; the six items are docs and regression-guard work.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 1, 2, 4 | Switch claims read against the resolver and the CLI/handler/launcher readers; each active P2 re-read at its cited line. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 1-4 | Switch paths, docs/scenario, switch tests and module map, and holdout hygiene each covered. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No runtime mirror changed in this area. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | 2 | `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:23` matches the CLI/file and daemon/own-env split. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial (one P2) | 2 | CP-003's control command is the one playbook defect (`iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases`). |\n\nHoldout hygiene: the three prompt files were read only through `jq -c 'del(.prompt)' | wc -l`; counts are 224, 63 and 36 rows. No prompt text appears in any iteration, delta, report or registry entry.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Cross-area switch readers**: the Python shim's `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`-only reader and the OpenCode plugin's reason-label fallback are outside the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` file list. They were checked as context and are recorded as edge cases, not findings. If a future pass reviews those files, the canonical-name question should be raised there.\n- **Command-offer fit on refusal/question/history/mention**: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` is not in the pass-five scope list, so it was not reviewed here. The brief's offer checks belong to the lineage whose area owns that module; this lineage reports no claim about it.\n- **Graph-backed convergence**: the coverage graph stayed unavailable across all four iterations. The run stops at `maxIterationsReached`; the final iteration's new-finding ratio is 0, but that is telemetry, not a graph-backed STOP.\n- **Performance and security hardening beyond the switch**: no workload or exploit path was named for the switch, so no performance or security finding was raised beyond the prompt-safety check in iteration 1.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Audit Appendix\n\n### Iteration Table\n\n| Iteration | Focus | Dimensions | New findings | Ratio | Verdict | Files written |\n|-----------|-------|------------|--------------|-------|---------|---------------|\n| 1 | Correctness and security of the switch | correctness, security | 0 | 0.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` |\n| 2 | Docs and scenario traceability | traceability | 3 P2 | 1.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-002.md`, `deltas/iter-002.jsonl` |\n| 3 | Switch tests and module map | maintainability | 3 P2 | 0.50 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-003.md`, `deltas/iter-003.jsonl` |\n| 4 | Stabilization and holdout hygiene | all four | 0 | 0.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-004.md`, `deltas/iter-004.jsonl` |\n\n### Coverage Matrix\n\n| File | Dimensions reviewed | Last iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|--------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts` | D1, D2, D3, D4 | 4 | 0 | complete |\n| `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\n| `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\n| `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | D1, D2, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\n| `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example` | D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\n| `manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md` | D3 | 4 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `runtime/lib/README.md` | D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts` | D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\n| `runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\n| `runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` | D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\n| `runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-test-utils.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md` | D3 | 2 | 2 P2 | complete |\n| Shared docs (`INSTALL-GUIDE`, feature catalog, changelog, hooks README) | D3 | 2 | 0 on their own claims | complete |\n\n### Convergence Replay\n\n- Resolver and readers re-read: `hook-flags.cjs:38-41,70-78,256-258`, `env-aliases.cjs:20-49`, `advisor-disabled.ts:74-93`, `skill-advisor-cli.ts:1540`, `advisor-recommend.ts:646`, `system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:312-315`.\n- Final registry: 0 P0, 0 P1, 6 P2; all four dimensions covered; `convergenceScore` 1 after the stabilization pass; `graphDecision` null, so the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\n- Read-only switch probes (no daemon started): `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1`, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=yes`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` each returned empty recommendations, `freshness: unavailable`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and an abstain reason naming the deciding switch. The control probe with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` reproduced `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases`.\n- No reviewed file was modified; every write landed inside `review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/`.\n\n### Dimension Breakdown\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration(s) | Note |\n|-----------|---------|--------------|------|\n| Correctness | pass | 1, 4 | The switch stops the CLI and handler before daemon/scorer I/O; the launcher filter is clean. |\n| Security | pass | 1, 4 | No prompt text in the disabled envelope; no switch bypass; the disabled path cannot reach an unvalidated workspace root. |\n| Traceability | pass with advisories | 2, 4 | Three P2 doc/scenario gaps; the feature catalog and changelog claims hold. |\n| Maintainability | pass with advisories | 3, 4 | Three P2 test/map gaps; the switch code is otherwise pinned at both boundaries. |\n\n**Overall verdict: PASS** (six P2 advisories; no P0 or P1 active).\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\":\"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build — kill-switch-cli-5 (pass five)\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: lineage=kill-switch-cli-5; sessionId=fanout-kill-switch-cli-5-1794760565927-i99t40; generation=1; lineageMode=new; stopReason=maxIterationsReached -->\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Overall verdict:** PASS\\n- **hasAdvisories:** true (six active P2 findings; no P0 or P1)\\n- **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 6\\n- **Review scope:** the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. The reviewed files are `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example`, the CP-003 manual scenario, `runtime/lib/README.md`, the four switch test files, the shared CLI test utils and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md`, plus the shared docs that describe them (`INSTALL-GUIDE.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md`).\\n- **Operator review focus:** pass-five code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-5.txt` first. Review the `kill-switch-cli` files plus docs that describe them. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal/question/history/mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open the three prompt files except through `jq del(.prompt)`; counts only. Change no code and write only inside the lineage folder.\\n- **Headline:** the kill switch and the direct-call switch work on every path this area claims. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, its aliases, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` and a flags-file entry all make the CLI abstain before any daemon starts or the scorer runs; the daemon handler abstains from its own environment; the launcher's exact-set child-env allowlist no longer carries a switch, so a flagged caller cannot silence later callers. The six active P2s are documentation and test-maintenance gaps: the env index's alias column contradicts the resolver, the advisor row's Source column omits the direct-call readers, CP-003's control command does not isolate the full alias set, the launcher switch fixture covers two of ten names, the CLI alias loop excludes every `MK_` name, and the lib module map omits five modules.\\n- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `converged` for this area: no active P0 or P1 remains, and the six P2s are advisories.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nNo remediation plan is required for this lineage: it has no active P0 or P1. The six P2s are advisories for a follow-up changelog/docs-maintenance pass.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": false,\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"PASS\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": true,\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": 6,\\n  \\\"nextCommand\\\": \\\"/create:changelog\\\",\\n  \\\"remediationWorkstreams\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"specSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"State the switch set as one table: canonical, aliases, master and the readers at the CLI, handler and prompt surfaces\\\",\\n    \\\"State the CP-003 isolation rule: the control call must unset every name the resolver honors, not only the four in the scenario\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"planSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"Fix ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75 and .skilled/hooks/README.md:44 to name the MK_ aliases and the direct-call readers\\\",\\n    \\\"Extend the CP-003 control command to unset SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED, SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED and the MK_ names\\\",\\n    \\\"Drive the launcher fixture from ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS instead of two literals\\\",\\n    \\\"Assert abstention for the three MK_ names in the CLI disable loop without asserting the exact reason string\\\",\\n    \\\"Refresh the runtime/lib/README.md directory tree against the real directory\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\n    \\\"traceability/alias-table\\\",\\n    \\\"traceability/source-column\\\",\\n    \\\"traceability/scenario-isolation\\\",\\n    \\\"maintainability/test-fixture\\\",\\n    \\\"maintainability/test-filter\\\",\\n    \\\"maintainability/module-map\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/hooks/README.md\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts\\\",\\n    \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": false\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Severity | Dimension | Title | Evidence | First / last seen | Status |\\n|----|----------|-----------|-------|----------|-------------------|--------|\\n| `iter2-P2-env-alias-column` | P2 | traceability | The master-switch row says \\\"No aliases\\\" while the resolver honors `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:38-41,256-258`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:20-33` | 2 / 4 | active |\\n| `iter2-P2-env-source-column` | P2 | traceability | The advisor switch row's Source column omits the direct-call readers it claims | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:75`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:70-93`; `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1540`; `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:646` | 2 / 4 | active |\\n| `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | P2 | traceability | CP-003's unflagged control call can abstain under a switch alias it never unsets | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49,80`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.cjs:41,70-78` | 2 / 4 | active |\\n| `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture` | P2 | maintainability | The launcher test covers two of the ten switch names it claims to keep out of the daemon env | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:124-145`; `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts:74-81` | 3 / 4 | active |\\n| `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter` | P2 | maintainability | The CLI disable loop filters out every `MK_` alias, so the direct-call path never exercises those names | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:219-221`; `.skilled/hooks/shared/env-aliases.cjs:20-49` | 3 / 4 | active |\\n| `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | P2 | maintainability | The lib README tree omits five flat modules that exist on disk | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:100-122,138-140` | 3 / 4 | active |\\n\\nEvery active finding carries a concrete input in its iteration narrative; none relies on inference alone. The resolver and the CLI/handler/launcher switch paths are clean.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n| Lane | Findings | Order | Work |\\n|------|----------|-------|------|\\n| A. Switch docs and scenario | `iter2-P2-env-alias-column`, `iter2-P2-env-source-column`, `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases` | 1 | Correct the env index's alias and Source columns against `MASTER_ALIASES`/`LEGACY_ALIASES`, add the MK_ names, name the CLI/handler readers, and unset the full alias set in CP-003's control command. |\\n| B. Switch tests and module map | `iter3-P2-launcher-switch-fixture`, `iter3-P2-cli-mk-alias-filter`, `iter3-P2-lib-readme-tree` | 2 | Drive the launcher fixture from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS`, stop excluding `MK_` from the CLI abstain loop, and refresh the lib tree from the directory. |\\n\\nLane A does not depend on Lane B; both are advisory and can land in one documentation-maintenance change.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- Record the switch set as one canonical table: `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, its aliases (including the `MK_` names), `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED`, and the readers (`runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, the CLI, the daemon handler, the prompt hook and the plugin).\\n- Record the disabled-envelope contract: empty recommendations, `freshness: unavailable`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED`, the deciding switch name, no prompt text, and the caller's workspace root.\\n- Record the launcher isolation rule: the daemon child env is an exact-set allowlist and never carries a switch name.\\n- Record the CP-003 control rule: the unflagged control call must unset every name the resolver honors, not only the four names in the current command.\\n- Add a `## Rule overrides`-free, plain note that the lib README tree is a file map and must list every flat module.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n1. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md:74-75` and `.skilled/hooks/README.md:44`: replace \\\"No aliases\\\" with the `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED` alias; add the three `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_*` names; add `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` and `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` to the advisor row's Source column.\\n2. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md:49`: extend the `env -u` list with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED` and `MK_HOOKS_DISABLED`.\\n3. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts:127-145`: build the source env from `ADVISOR_DISABLED_FLAGS` so all ten names are filtered, keeping the exact-set assertion.\\n4. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:221`: include the three `MK_` names and assert `recommendations: []` and `daemon.calls.length === 0` for them; assert the exact reason only for the names whose string is stable.\\n5. Edit `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/README.md:100-122`: add `caller-context.ts`, `compiled-routing-flag.ts`, `df-idf.ts`, `private-skill-target.ts` and `route-exclusions.ts`, and align the key-files table with the tree.\\n\\nNo source change is required for the switch behavior itself; the six items are docs and regression-guard work.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pass | 1, 2, 4 | Switch claims read against the resolver and the CLI/handler/launcher readers; each active P2 re-read at its cited line. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pass | 1-4 | Switch paths, docs/scenario, switch tests and module map, and holdout hygiene each covered. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | notApplicable | 1 | No runtime mirror changed in this area. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pass | 2 | `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:23` matches the CLI/file and daemon/own-env split. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | partial (one P2) | 2 | CP-003's control command is the one playbook defect (`iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases`). |\\n\\nHoldout hygiene: the three prompt files were read only through `jq -c 'del(.prompt)' | wc -l`; counts are 224, 63 and 36 rows. No prompt text appears in any iteration, delta, report or registry entry.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Cross-area switch readers**: the Python shim's `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED`-only reader and the OpenCode plugin's reason-label fallback are outside the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` file list. They were checked as context and are recorded as edge cases, not findings. If a future pass reviews those files, the canonical-name question should be raised there.\\n- **Command-offer fit on refusal/question/history/mention**: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` is not in the pass-five scope list, so it was not reviewed here. The brief's offer checks belong to the lineage whose area owns that module; this lineage reports no claim about it.\\n- **Graph-backed convergence**: the coverage graph stayed unavailable across all four iterations. The run stops at `maxIterationsReached`; the final iteration's new-finding ratio is 0, but that is telemetry, not a graph-backed STOP.\\n- **Performance and security hardening beyond the switch**: no workload or exploit path was named for the switch, so no performance or security finding was raised beyond the prompt-safety check in iteration 1.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Iteration Table\\n\\n| Iteration | Focus | Dimensions | New findings | Ratio | Verdict | Files written |\\n|-----------|-------|------------|--------------|-------|---------|---------------|\\n| 1 | Correctness and security of the switch | correctness, security | 0 | 0.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-001.md`, `deltas/iter-001.jsonl` |\\n| 2 | Docs and scenario traceability | traceability | 3 P2 | 1.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-002.md`, `deltas/iter-002.jsonl` |\\n| 3 | Switch tests and module map | maintainability | 3 P2 | 0.50 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-003.md`, `deltas/iter-003.jsonl` |\\n| 4 | Stabilization and holdout hygiene | all four | 0 | 0.00 | PASS | `iterations/iteration-004.md`, `deltas/iter-004.jsonl` |\\n\\n### Coverage Matrix\\n\\n| File | Dimensions reviewed | Last iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|--------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts` | D1, D2, D3, D4 | 4 | 0 | complete |\\n| `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\\n| `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | D1, D2, D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\\n| `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | D1, D2, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\\n| `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example` | D3 | 2 | 0 | complete |\\n| `manual-testing-playbook/compat-and-disable/global-disable-flag.md` | D3 | 4 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `runtime/lib/README.md` | D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `runtime/tests/advisor-disabled.vitest.ts` | D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\\n| `runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\\n| `runtime/tests/launcher-bootstrap.vitest.ts` | D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 1 P2 | complete |\\n| `runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-test-utils.ts` | D1, D4 | 3 | 0 | complete |\\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md` | D3 | 2 | 2 P2 | complete |\\n| Shared docs (`INSTALL-GUIDE`, feature catalog, changelog, hooks README) | D3 | 2 | 0 on their own claims | complete |\\n\\n### Convergence Replay\\n\\n- Resolver and readers re-read: `hook-flags.cjs:38-41,70-78,256-258`, `env-aliases.cjs:20-49`, `advisor-disabled.ts:74-93`, `skill-advisor-cli.ts:1540`, `advisor-recommend.ts:646`, `system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:312-315`.\\n- Final registry: 0 P0, 0 P1, 6 P2; all four dimensions covered; `convergenceScore` 1 after the stabilization pass; `graphDecision` null, so the stop reason is `maxIterationsReached`.\\n- Read-only switch probes (no daemon started): `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1`, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1`, `SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED=yes`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED=1` and `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` each returned empty recommendations, `freshness: unavailable`, `ADVISOR_DISABLED` and an abstain reason naming the deciding switch. The control probe with `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_PLUGIN_DISABLED=1` reproduced `iter2-P2-cp003-control-aliases`.\\n- No reviewed file was modified; every write landed inside `review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/`.\\n\\n### Dimension Breakdown\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration(s) | Note |\\n|-----------|---------|--------------|------|\\n| Correctness | pass | 1, 4 | The switch stops the CLI and handler before daemon/scorer I/O; the launcher filter is clean. |\\n| Security | pass | 1, 4 | No prompt text in the disabled envelope; no switch bypass; the disabled path cannot reach an unvalidated workspace root. |\\n| Traceability | pass with advisories | 2, 4 | Three P2 doc/scenario gaps; the feature catalog and changelog claims hold. |\\n| Maintainability | pass with advisories | 3, 4 | Three P2 test/map gaps; the switch code is otherwise pinned at both boundaries. |\\n\\n**Overall verdict: PASS** (six P2 advisories; no P0 or P1 active).\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794761855978,"end":1794761895339}}}}
