{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794762085897,"sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","part":{"partID":"prt_1e0280dd0001AWlg2FOtD3MB6Y","sessionID":"ses_e1feefdd5ffeS4J0KdMtC6TlEK","messageID":"msg_1e027f729001E61W7MC7BLF4z2","type":"tool","id":"call_148677d52fcc4f9d9feac162","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `in-progress`: the state follows the stop reason, not the verdict, so this run does not claim the graph-backed `converged` state even though no active P0 or P1 remains. The six P2s are advisories.","oldString":"- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `converged` for this area: no active P0 or P1 remains, and the six P2s are advisories.","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md\n@@ -9,9 +9,9 @@\n - **Active findings:** P0 = 0, P1 = 0, P2 = 6\n - **Review scope:** the pass-five `kill-switch-cli` area of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`. The reviewed files are `runtime/lib/advisor-disabled.ts`, `runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts`, `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, `.skilled/bin/system-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs`, `.skilled/hooks/hook-flags.env.example`, the CP-003 manual scenario, `runtime/lib/README.md`, the four switch test files, the shared CLI test utils and `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/ENV-REFERENCE.md`, plus the shared docs that describe them (`INSTALL-GUIDE.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `changelog/v1.1.0.0.md`, `.skilled/hooks/README.md`).\n - **Operator review focus:** pass-five code review of command surfacing. Read `review-brief-5.txt` first. Review the `kill-switch-cli` files plus docs that describe them. Check the kill switch and direct-call switch paths, command offers on refusal/question/history/mention, Vibe journal scoring, the doctor hooks-file reading, docs against code, and holdout hygiene. Never open the three prompt files except through `jq del(.prompt)`; counts only. Change no code and write only inside the lineage folder.\n - **Headline:** the kill switch and the direct-call switch work on every path this area claims. `SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DISABLED`, its aliases, `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` and a flags-file entry all make the CLI abstain before any daemon starts or the scorer runs; the daemon handler abstains from its own environment; the launcher's exact-set child-env allowlist no longer carries a switch, so a flagged caller cannot silence later callers. The six active P2s are documentation and test-maintenance gaps: the env index's alias column contradicts the resolver, the advisor row's Source column omits the direct-call readers, CP-003's control command does not isolate the full alias set, the launcher switch fixture covers two of ten names, the CLI alias loop excludes every `MK_` name, and the lib module map omits five modules.\n-- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `converged` for this area: no active P0 or P1 remains, and the six P2s are advisories.\n+- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `in-progress`: the state follows the stop reason, not the verdict, so this run does not claim the graph-backed `converged` state even though no active P0 or P1 remains. The six P2s are advisories.\n \n ---\n \n ## 2. Planning Trigger\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `in-progress`: the state follows the stop reason, not the verdict, so this run does not claim the graph-backed `converged` state even though no active P0 or P1 remains. The six P2s are advisories.\",\"oldString\":\"- **Loop state:** four iterations completed; all four dimensions covered; the final stabilization pass found no new finding. The legal stop reason is `maxIterationsReached` because the coverage graph was unavailable and no graph-backed convergence decision exists. Release readiness is `converged` for this area: no active P0 or P1 remains, and the six P2s are advisories.\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/kill-switch-cli-5/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794762083792,"end":1794762085897}}}}
